{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie","id":649866,"title":"Two questions from a Vampire newbie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-03T02:39:51-07:00","id":649866,"title":"Two questions from a Vampire newbie","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I have Vampire: the Requiem book at home, but I have yet to play or GM it. Nevertheless, I tried considered both - and there are two questions that I struggle with:<br /> <br /> 1. When coming up with possible characters, I started to wonder: why would anyone actually decide to become a vampire? I mean... being vampire obviously sucks, because you have to literally prey on human beings. Wouldn't that turn almost anyone off the idea of allowing themselves to be Embraced? It would seem to me that only complete psychopaths and very desperate people would be willing to become vampires... How do you have your characters rationalize it, then?<br /> <br /> 2. When I was considering GM this game, I realized that I... have no idea what Vampire games could actually be about. It's a very rich setting, but what stories can you actually tell in it? Could you share any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T03:09:58-07:00","id":649894,"title":"","content":"1. Immortality (for young people - being young forever, for older people - not dying), power - being strong, fast, virtually indestructible etc., amazing tricks - dominate, majesty, obfuscate - who doesn't want to be able to hypnotize people at will <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And those are just three possible things. I assume that for each person it would be something different, but if given the choice I guess that most people would at least seriously consider it.<br /> 2. You can make it about whatever you want - politics is usually the favourite, but there are some alternatives:<br /> love separated by the embrace<br /> loneliness (you can't really hang around your old friends anymore)<br /> madness (you become too strong for your own good)<br /> or just good old detective game, where your prince asks you to figure out a mystery and you have to use your powers to find the guilty person or a missing object.<br /> Again, obviously these are just some of the things you could use, and perhaps you'll have the most fun when you use them all in one game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/640-bram_pc","name":"Bram_pc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T03:23:15-07:00","id":649898,"title":"","content":"Entirely not the person to be answering, having not read the book, but can people not simply be tricked, seduced, or otherwise manipulated into becoming a Vampire?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you have your standard bunch: I'm dying and want a way out, I'm an utter hedonist and this sounds jolly fun, I want revenge on someone, I'm suicidally depressed and can't be bothered saying no, I have low self-esteem and this is how I'm punishing myself, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T03:39:52-07:00","id":649901,"title":"","content":"In addition to the stated answers to #1, there's the obvious: a lot of them don't. If a vampire has decided to Embrace you, there's little you can really do to stop it. Posthumous Embraces and second edition's revenants reinforce that further. Once you have already been Embraced, it becomes a very different question, because now it's about personal survival and the fear of eternal death. Even if you don't want to spend eternity as a parasite, it takes a great deal of courage to intentionally leave yourself out for the sun. And the taste of sating the hunger is seductive. It becomes easy to rationalize to yourself over the years. Maybe you can live a good enough unlife that you can make up for what damage you do. Maybe you can feed relatively safely, on willing vessels or on vermin, and get by that way. From there, the temptations start by inches.<br /> <br /> Most of those old, callous elder vampires started out as relatively reasonable, empathetic people. But they got put into a situation designed to turn men into monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T03:43:05-07:00","id":649903,"title":"","content":"The Embrace isn't usually performed with the consent of the character that is about to be made a vampire. The character is turned into a vampire because their sire WANTS them to become a vampire. They are the ones who are consciously throwing away part of their own soul in the form of Humanity to turn someone else into a vampire. So the real question is more along the lines of why did their sire want an individual to become a vampire? And that, more often than not, is for personal and utterly self centered reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T04:17:33-07:00","id":649923,"title":"","content":"The vast majority of consensual embraces are probably of mortals that are already in the vampiric fold. Ghouls and blood dolls who see it as a promotion to the ranks of the Masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T04:33:25-07:00","id":649939,"title":"","content":"I'd do it. Hands down. For the sake of answering your question, here's why (plus a few extras):<br /> You don't actually have to hurt anyone. You can feed from animals. Even if you don't, there are plenty of people that would willingly get bit once they know what it feels like. It's not harm if its consent. Now, if you feed from more than animals, there's a chance you'll kill someone. The chance gets bigger as you get older. But you can minimize that chance, and you also have a chance to kill someone just driving your car. A lot of people on this forum seem to disagree with me on the &quot;you can feed without harming&quot; thing, but the point is I believe it. It's pretty clear that there are others in the World of Darkness who could believe the same. Given that this is a matter of reasons and rationals, I'd like to avoid yet another debate on the matter.<br /> <br /> in addition, there's the promise of a world that few people have ever seen. The World of Darkness so to speak. There are people driven by curiosity, especially towards the unlives of something so iconic as the vampire. Imagine the interviewer in Interview with a Vampire. Anne Rice vampires seem to have it far worse for far less benefit in the movie than VtR vampires, and he still jumped at the chance. There are also people desperately in need of the idea that there's more to this world than the daily toil of a 9-5 until you retire and then die. Vampires prove that there's more to this world. Being one provides an escape from that drudgery.<br /> <br /> There's always wealth and power (physical and mystical) and immortality, too. Fear of death is potent.<br /> <br /> As other people have mentioned, there's nothing that says you have to consent.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, perhaps: Nobody ever said that your Sire had to be completely honest before he or she sires you. That'd be breaching Masquerade a bit too far for someone who isn't a vampire. There are so many myths about being a vampire that the average human doesn't really know what it entails until they're told or they experience it themselves. Nobody says they have to be told before they're sired.<br /> <br /> As for campaign ideas?<br /> For VtR I usually have Neonates doing the bidding of their elders. Investigating Masquerade breaches are one. Investigating in general, really. One player is Ordo Dracul. He gets sent to a Wyrm's Nest by his boss. The other players are sent along to make sure that the Ordo isn't overstepping their bounds by keeping forbidden Lancea knowledge or whatever. A Revenant is raised and attacking unaware Kine. The players have to find him and deliver him to Final Death or maybe the Prince if the Prince needs him alive for some reason.<br /> <br /> That's if you need a more standard &quot;quest&quot;-based campaign. A lot of people have suggested to me that you should make a roster of NPCs, give them all aspirations, then set the PCs loose. Between the NPC aspirations giving them reasons to ask the PCs for help and the PCs aspirations giving them reasons to ask the NPCs for help, you should have what you need. The benefit to this method is you'll probably have more time for dealing with Touchstones and whatever personal projects the PCs want. The downside is you can probably give up on the idea of keeping the party together all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T04:58:07-07:00","id":649955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=649939#post649939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd do it. Hands down. For the sake of answering your question, here's why (plus a few extras):<br /> You don't actually have to hurt anyone. You can feed from animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really Feeding off animals under Blood &amp; Smoke is time consuming. By My Calculations 7 Gallons blood from cattle for 6 vitae vs 11 pints from a human for 7.<br /> One definitely has a higher kick.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/305707-what-s-the-blood-economy-like-in-your-games?p=307643#post307643\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...643#post307643</a><br /> <br /> As to the question. Assuming you are given a choice a lot of people are kicked around and put upon.<br /> An offer of power and to settle the score is very tempting to most people whether we admit it or not.<br /> The power to take out the high school bully or the cop shaking you down.<br /> If you are a woman and you want to beat the jock who assaulted you to bloody pulp and a vamp offers you the dark gift, are you going to say no?<br /> <br /> As to games? How many players?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T05:39:47-07:00","id":649980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=649955#post649955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really Feeding off animals under Blood &amp; Smoke is time consuming. By My Calculations 7 Gallons blood from cattle for 6 vitae vs 11 pints from a human for 7.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant. They get one <i>vitae</i> per turn. The volume of blood that corresponds to isn't a factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T05:54:38-07:00","id":649990,"title":"","content":"Also irrelevant since this isn't about mechanics but why one would willingly become a vampire. Like I said in my post. That Chattnos should have read before responding. This turns into a derailing debate every damn time, even when I explicitly try to avoid it. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T05:56:48-07:00","id":649992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=649980#post649980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Irrelevant. They get one <i>vitae</i> per turn. The volume of blood that corresponds to isn't a factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does mean you're exsanguinating about two pigs a week just to keep out of torpor, though, not counting any vitae you have to replenish from healing or discipline use. I mean, that seems inconvenient even with Animalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T06:27:14-07:00","id":650003,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about some character concepts and energy conservation and it doesn't say you <i>have </i>to wake up. So if you were a party person you could just wake up on Friday and Saturday nights. That way you wouldn't waste time and Vitae.<br /> <br /> I'd probably do it myself. Immortality is a big draw, magic powers help. But as stated above most people don't really have a choice. It's the vampire that decides for them. I was reading the Beast Within anthology and the first story was a tale about a girl with no place left to go begging a vampire to turn her because of it, while he gnashes and snarls over the decision because he wants to but it's against the Prince's rules. It seemed silly the vampire didn't think of the third option, ghouling, which was likely allowed, would have brought the girl into the All Night's Society but not cursed her. It was a Masquerade book so the curse angle was played up more.<br /> <br /> Now, appreciating that a vampire didn't necessarily choose to become a vampire, as for what vampire games are about, at the basics you have, 'What do you do when you're dead?' How do you spend your Requiem. Ideally for me, a storyteller weaves a tale to tempt and challenge your vampire's mindset on that. Is your vampire going to decide to only eat animals? Are they willing to do the bidding of the Collective, who control local pounds and slaughterhouses, to do so? Especially when, after that last frenzy, human blood tastes <i>so </i>good, and it's all around you in easy-to-drink containers practically begging to be popped open. Look at Mia, she's so commanding and confident, she doesn't scrounge in alleys sucking on rats, maybe she's got the right way about it. And repercussions and consequences are highlighted, what happens when the Collective decides one job isn't enough? Or it turns out the victim of your last frenzy is part of a werewolf pack and now you're hunted and might need to increase your vitae supply just to survive. And of course I like to throw in an overarching story or two that doesn't focus on the characters in particular but serves to highlight themes of vampire or the location they're in or other things, like the inter-covenant warring leading to a head and an all-out war, an usurper to the title of Prince, a drastic change of policy that may change the vampire's city as they know it completely, for better or worse.<br /> <br /> But that's just how I do it, there's really a lot of ways to go about that sort of thing, a story can place an emphasis on the vampire's attempts to cling to their human life despite their changes, a 'quest' of sorts to find their sire and stare them down as you ask them, 'Why?' or any number of stories with any number of ways to tell. You don't even have to limit it to vampires and can throw some other supernatural templates into the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T09:16:40-07:00","id":650212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie#post649866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. When coming up with possible characters, I started to wonder: why would anyone actually decide to become a vampire? I mean... being vampire obviously sucks, because you have to literally prey on human beings. Wouldn't that turn almost anyone off the idea of allowing themselves to be Embraced? It would seem to me that only complete psychopaths and very desperate people would be willing to become vampires... How do you have your characters rationalize it, then?</div> </div> </div> </div> One, you don't need to be a psychopath to be willing to kill someone to survive yourself. Serial killers come from all walks of life, and for many reasons, not just psychosis. And the pay out is rather nice - immortality. So, no. The thought of preying on another human won't turn off people from being a vampire. Its a cost, yes, but not one that people can't live with. If you want to really get into it, there's a significant number of people that leech off others for their own wealth and prosperity - just this week, we have a Detroit city priest arrested for embezzling money from a church that was earmarked for charity work. Drug dealers kill people with poison for money. We can make some comparisons to the really wealthy if we wanted to.<br /> <br /> Two, when you're young and newly vampized, you can live off animal blood. Or avoid killing people if you're strong enough of will. Sure, it will eventually happen at some point. But the feeling is that, if you're careful, you can avoid it. Eventually, over time, you come to peace with drinking from humans as your mind changes over time.<br /> <br /> Three, people glamorize the upsides and downplay the drawbacks. Immortality and disciplines are very nice. As is immunity to disease - if you're dying and don't believe in an afterlife, undeath seems like a pretty awesome alternative to not living at all. There are lots of positives to being a vampire, and its hard to really understand the drawbacks without experiencing them. <br /> <br /> Four, you can become a vampire in any number of ways. There's the revenants/larvae that rise from overfeeding, there are post mortem embraces, there are embraces where your sire is punishing you. Maybe you were a ghoul for a long time and its become too much of a strain to maintain that state, and time to try something new instead of dying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. When I was considering GM this game, I realized that I... have no idea what Vampire games could actually be about. It's a very rich setting, but what stories can you actually tell in it? Could you share any ideas? </div> </div> </div> There's plenty of possibilities. Vampires live in the dark side of humanity, the seething underbelly of crime, taboo desires, drugs, abuse, and rampant sexuality. The slow slide away from humanity into predator. There's the politics, trying to find feeding grounds, the struggle of opposing philosophy. A new way to explore the new World you've been shown. A struggle of dark forces against pure evil (Brood, VII). Explore how necessary evils are needed for society to thrive. Use vampires as metaphors for modern racial concerns. I've done games where vampires came out of the coffin and were revealed to the public at large. That was fun. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T14:25:40-07:00","id":650578,"title":"","content":"Okay, thanks for all the ideas for stories <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Although I could use more... the more, the better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the issue of Embrace - so, how many people end up Embraced against their will? Somehow, I ended up coming to the conclusion that they are the minority. Am I wrong?<br /> <br /> BTW. Which sourcebooks would you consider the most useful for a vampire GM? Are the covenant books useful? The clan books? Something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T14:49:59-07:00","id":650594,"title":"","content":"It's going to depend on your game, but the default assumption is that most people aren't Embraced with any awareness of vampires, let alone given a decision about it. Revenants aren't even made on purpose, they're the result of vampires draining someone dry who just happens to rise as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Vampire second edition, the clanbooks, Damnation City, and Secrets of the Covenants. I'm fond of Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners and Belial's Brood as well but the latter may not be applicable in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-03-2015, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T15:07:25-07:00","id":650617,"title":"","content":"Well, I plan on playing the first edition for now, because it's the book I own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T15:24:56-07:00","id":650640,"title":"","content":"In that case, the clan books, Belial's Brood and VII, Damnation City, both Night Horrors books, Invite Only and the Danse Macabre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T15:27:41-07:00","id":650645,"title":"","content":"What about the covenant books? I admit they would be my first choice, as the covenant descriptions in the core rulebook are really brief (for once, it's not actually explained what Lancea Sanctum's religion really is...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T15:34:15-07:00","id":650651,"title":"","content":"There's some interesting stuff there, but it's such dry reading and a lot of it is going to be superfluous. You can probably find the relevant information compiled online. A couple websites seem to be gathering all the 'important' parts of the games fluff and mechanics on wikis. Plus you'll probably be able to apply the information in the upcoming Secrets of the Covenants to a first edition game. They're using the clanbook style approach to writing it so, at the least, it will be easier to read.<br /> <br /> Those recommendations are just my advice, others will probably recommend lists they find more useful..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T15:48:20-07:00","id":650677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=650578#post650578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the issue of Embrace - so, how many people end up Embraced against their will? Somehow, I ended up coming to the conclusion that they are the minority. Am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Salt to taste; this is one that can vary a lot between game tables as needed and there's not really a wrong answer. My assumption has always been that the majority of Embraces were not able to make an informed decision, for any number of reasons:<ul><li>They arose as a vampire without a direct sire, spontaneously. This is rare and unusual, but possible.</li> <li>They were dead or dying, and were given the Embrace either because a manipulative sire found them a convenient choice who would be indebted to her, or a caring sire wanted to save and preserve them and the Embrace seemed the only way to do so.</li> <li>They were outright Embraced against their will, such as a ghoul being Embraced by an enemy of his sire to be used as a weapon against her, or a mad vampire in the mountains Embracing prey who impress him with their ability to survive his predations for a long chase, as a perverse reward or to nurture a challenge to relish.</li> <li>A sire found them interesting and desired them at her side as a friend, an aide, a proteg\u00e9, a patsy, or whatever, but didn't fill them in on the whole deal. They probably knew their sire had some strange power or inhuman aura, but not necessarily that she was a vampire. She might give them a vaguely worded, mysterious offer to mull over, or even secretly arrange a circumstance that would leave the fledgling no choice but to accept.</li> </ul><br /> I consider that last entry, the incomplete-information offer, the likely most frequent scenario for how most surviving vampires get Embraced. (Some Embraces, like those that are inadvertant or coercive, might also be plentiful, but vampires Embraced under those circumstances are less likely to unlive as long as those eased into it and not born straight into a turf war.) The likely second most frequent, in my mind, is a ghoul of several years' service being chosen to receive the Embrace, already having been inculcated with an unnatural loyalty to his regnant and familiarity with vampiric society. A ghoul is likely to just view the deal as a step up.<br /> <br /> In general, being inducted into the ranks of the Kindred is a shady deal. Their society is a respectable veneer of etiquette and grandeur concealing a room of thugs with knives. Like the mob, often by the time you realize how deep you're in, you're already too deep to get back out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=650578#post650578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW. Which sourcebooks would you consider the most useful for a vampire GM? Are the covenant books useful? The clan books? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>#1 most useful: Damnation City.</b> Some GMs may find it less useful than others (it's not that useful to me personally), but if you're the kind of person wondering what <i>happens</i> in a Vampire game, how do you set up stakes and what kind of interesting events could ensue, this book is for you. It's a big old toolkit running down how to build a domain from the macro to the micro level, with lots of looks at different aspects of life in different sorts of cities for the Kindred. Take a look at the section on sample Princes; they're not individual NPC writeups so much as each writeup is an entire campaign setting and genre of game to run.<br /> <br /> <b>#2 most useful: The clanbooks.</b> The clanbooks are majority in-world artifact letters and writings \u2013 they're literal books about each clan that a character could ostensibly find in play and get caught up in. Each book tends to follow the story of a figure iconic of that clan, but is richly interspersed with episodic writings, vague historical references, and apocrypha associated with the themes and history of the clan. Each one also has a short appendix of mechanical widgets to play with. Let me put it this way: I didn't like Requiem until I first read one of the clanbooks (Mekhet: Shadows in the Dark). I'm not even normally a fan of this kind of in-character fiction in game writing. But these books do an excellent job of establishing through implication a defined world of uncertainty, forgotten omens, lonely monsters and secret betrayals. They contain vignettes that will show you what awful things a vampire does and why they are interesting. They're not humorless, either. Two of the Daeva clanbook's most biting spreads are given in the form of underground comic tracts.<br /> <br /> Past that, your mileage may vary. Depending on what you find interesting, you may look into Mythologies (alternate twists and strangeness associated with the nature of the Curse), Ancient Mysteries (on the psychology and behavior of elder vampires, and a collection of strange flashpoints in history as they relate to the Kindred), one of the covenant books, one of the Night Horrors books (Immortal Sinners for a rogue's gallery of trouble-stirring vampiric monsters, Wicked Dead for alien threats: vampires that are not Kindred, and Kindred that are not vampires), or something else entirely. These depend on your tastes and what kind of game you are interested in running, but Damnation City and the clanbooks are pretty universally recommendable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T15:50:08-07:00","id":650678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=650578#post650578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, thanks for all the ideas for stories <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Although I could use more... the more, the better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the issue of Embrace - so, how many people end up Embraced against their will? Somehow, I ended up coming to the conclusion that they are the minority. Am I wrong?<br /> <br /> BTW. Which sourcebooks would you consider the most useful for a vampire GM? Are the covenant books useful? The clan books? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For first edition bare bones minimum I would say the World of Darkness, Vampire the Requiem, and Damnation City. Anything else I recommend would be based on the answers to the following questions:<br /> 1. How much money do you have/want to spend?<br /> 2. What kind of chronicle(s) do you plan to run and do you want a lot of house rules or variants from the default setting?<br /> 3. What sort of characters are your players going to be drawn toward playing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T15:54:40-07:00","id":650681,"title":"","content":"Im suprised the two posters above me didn't mention The Blood. <br /> <br /> Damnation City is amazing for world building<br /> <br /> The Blood is amazing read to understanding Vampires so building npc's and a metric tone of adding flavor for both GM and PC. <br /> <br /> The clan books are optional compared to The Blood (my personal opinion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T16:01:12-07:00","id":650693,"title":"","content":"I'm not personally that big on the covenant books either, I think they tend to be dry. They did lay groundwork that later supplements ran with rather successfully, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=650645#post650645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(for once, it's not actually explained what Lancea Sanctum's religion really is...).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lancea et Sanctum <i>is</i> a religion. They're not Catholic, or Orthodox, or Protestant, or Jewish or Islamic or what have you. They resemble denominations of Christianity, especially Catholic due to their emergence during the decline of Rome, but their beliefs are distinct enough that most Christians would probably consider them offensively blasphemous. They believe that vampires are God's chosen scourges, at once cursed with damnation and blessed with holy duties to predate upon humanity, to test the pious and punish the wretched. They have their own Dark Father whom they arguably hold in higher regard than Jesus, shepherd of the dead as Christ was shepherd to the living.<br /> <br /> They're not vampires following a human faith. Their spiritual answers address the problems of the Requiem. And they start to sound really scary and unpleasant when you look at them from the perspective of those God commands them to eat and harry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T06:06:15-07:00","id":651081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=649990#post649990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also irrelevant since this isn't about mechanics but why one would willingly become a vampire. Like I said in my post. That Chattnos should have read before responding. This turns into a derailing debate every damn time, even when I explicitly try to avoid it. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh contraire.<br /> It is relevant. If you compare Blood &amp; Smokes rules to say Masquerade on blood banking and feeding off animals, it is clear they were trying to diminish those options.<br /> Blood Banking under B&amp;S Rules for elders is almost pointless.<br /> Now can you change the rules at your table to make easier in the setting. But that was not the intention of the designers.<br /> And I did address his question if you had read all of my response.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T07:01:17-07:00","id":651114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=650645#post650645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the covenant books? I admit they would be my first choice, as the covenant descriptions in the core rulebook are really brief (for once, it's not actually explained what Lancea Sanctum's religion really is...).</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually liked the crone book. Haven't delved in the others as much. But I guess I need to.<br /> YThe Clan Books are awesome. They really one of the better selections of the series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T08:39:07-07:00","id":651242,"title":"","content":"I admit that I have the Ventrue clanbook at home and... I didn't make it through it. Maybe I was too quick to jump to conclusions, but there was too much in-universe vague tidbits and not enough straight facts about what the Clan is like...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T10:17:25-07:00","id":651460,"title":"","content":"Ventrue are big on vague tidbits and avoiding straight facts. It doesn't help that they are arguably masters of mind control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T10:38:16-07:00","id":651469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=651242#post651242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit that I have the Ventrue clanbook at home and... I didn't make it through it. Maybe I was too quick to jump to conclusions, but there was too much in-universe vague tidbits and not enough straight facts about what the Clan is like...</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to think the Ventrue book is the driest of the bunch, but if anything it has much more in the way of straight facts than the clanbooks that follow, what with all of the sections on things like proper etiquette or the tale of Troy. The clanbooks are all about presentation through examples, show-don't-tell \u2013 here's what a Ventrue looks like when he comes out of lowly roots (the Lord of Paradise Lake), here's what a successful young Ventrue looks like (the Mogul), here's an outre spiritualist Ventrue (the Witch of the Woods), and here are some of the sides the Ventrue try not to show and how they end up coming out anyway (the dead girl's ritual, Malkavia). You notice the ways in which they differ and the ways in which they still resemble one another, and that's your picture of the clan. Requiem clans are neither monolithic nor do they tend to hang together in coherent political blocs. They're not covenants; they're tendencies and natures. That can be expressed a lot of different ways.<br /> <br /> Maybe give one of the later clanbooks a glance and see if you still feel like you don't get much out of it. Gangrel and Mekhet have central narratives about particular characters to wind the digressions around, and Nosferatu ties around exploring the mysteries and unfolding intrigue of a particular domain in a violent power struggle, so those might possibly give you something to hang onto. If they're still just not really your speed, then maybe it's just a fair cop. I can still recommend Damnation City even if you don't like the clanbooks, it's a much more traditional format for a supplement book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T12:17:42-07:00","id":651612,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the recommendations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll give the Ventrue book a second chance.<br /> <br /> I'm also reaaaaally tempted by the covenant books, as I really don't think that the core rulebook gives enough information on them. As I said, it doesn't explain a lot about Lancea Sanctum's dogma - and it also doesn't say a lot about Ordo Dracul philosophy or Crone's beliefs. How can people RP characters from these covenant with so little information, I wonder?<br /> <br /> BTW. Is there a book that deals with gargoyles? There are another part of the core book that I find frustrating. They are mentioned, but there's no rules for them as to how to create one...<br /> <br /> BTW 2. What's your opinion on the Bloodlines books?<br /> <br /> And to answer Tsusazi's question:<br /> <br /> 1. I don't have too much money right now, but I hope to have more in the future <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So, I'm gathering intel about possible purchases <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. I have no idea what kind of chronicle I would like to run... Right now, I'd just like to learn more about the default setting.<br /> <br /> 3. I have no prospective players right now, so I don't know what they would be playing. Still, I would like to be ready for anything...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T12:27:00-07:00","id":651616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=651612#post651612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also reaaaaally tempted by the covenant books, as I really don't think that the core rulebook gives enough information on them. As I said, it doesn't explain a lot about Lancea Sanctum's dogma - and it also doesn't say a lot about Ordo Dracul philosophy or Crone's beliefs. How can people RP characters from these covenant with so little information, I wonder?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking the information from the core and other books and running with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW. Is there a book that deals with gargoyles? There are another part of the core book that I find frustrating. They are mentioned, but there's no rules for them as to how to create one... </div> </div> </div>The Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW 2. What's your opinion on the Bloodlines books? </div> </div> </div>Some nice ideas mixed in with things you'll never want to use. A problem with all the z-splat books, I think. What people find nice ideas and things they'll never want to use vary from person to person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T12:44:51-07:00","id":651660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=651612#post651612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW. Is there a book that deals with gargoyles? There are another part of the core book that I find frustrating. They are mentioned, but there's no rules for them as to how to create one...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Circle of the Crone book has some Cruac rituals to raise gargoyles. The Danse Macabre, a big book of miscellaneous hacks, alternatives and optional rules, probably has the best section on gargoyles with an eye towards their use in play, general rules for creating them and several variant types associated with the different clans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=651612#post651612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW 2. What's your opinion on the Bloodlines books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Super hit-and-miss. If I were to rank them according to personal preference, I'd go Ancient Bloodlines &gt; The Chosen &gt; The Hidden &gt; The Legendary. Many of them, especially as you go further to the right in my list, are very high-concept. Sometimes this works (insect-like vampires who organize their servants into hive-like colonies, tragically comic pop culture aficionados who are more invested in using their power to seem glamorous than to actually wheel and deal, an insular and distrustful bloodline that sets up in families in rural areas), and sometimes they just come off as silly (the smell vampires who obsessively kidnap people with smells, the body-part-exchanging circus performers). Chosen has a few that are a bit more fleshed out and three-dimensional. I like the Agonistes, researchers and historians who labor to keep knowledge from falling into the fog of torpor, but are especially tempted by the pull of sleep themselves, and the Yagnatia, lordly pre-Christian Slavic Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> If you were to get just one of these books I'd go for Ancient Bloodlines. It's structured to match the historical flashpoints in Ancient Mysteries, with each flashpoint receiving two associated bloodlines born out of or active in that period, plus one miscellaneous write-up of something else (so it's not just a book solely of bloodlines). That includes a new variant of blood sorcery, a syncretic covenant of Buddhist vampires from Thailand, and the Edimmu, strange and vengeful ancient spirits, each seven in number, which inhabit the Kindred as a means of destroying them. Some of the bloodlines are good too: ancient Egyptians who remain loyal to the old gods but have lost their proper memories of the gods to the Fog of Ages and search to recover it; gnostic Gangrel who seek mad and holy wisdom from the voice of the Beast; mad emperors whose blood harbors a malevolent demon urging them to sate their hunger for souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T12:54:06-07:00","id":651676,"title":"","content":"Ha! I actually have Ancient Bloodlines and Ancient Mysteries <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> From what I've managed to read, they are indeed interesting. As for the rest of the Bloodline books, I've heard that The Legendary is the worst of them, with not many sensible ideas...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T17:08:56-07:00","id":651938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=651660#post651660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Circle of the Crone book has some Cruac rituals to raise gargoyles. The Danse Macabre, a big book of miscellaneous hacks, alternatives and optional rules, probably has the best section on gargoyles with an eye towards their use in play, general rules for creating them and several variant types associated with the different clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I liked Danse Macabre, I did not care for the gargoyles in that one. It seemed to imply to me at least clans could create them without cruac.<br /> Which to me is stealing some of the CoC's thunder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T17:11:46-07:00","id":651940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=651676#post651676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ha! I actually have Ancient Bloodlines and Ancient Mysteries <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> From what I've managed to read, they are indeed interesting. As for the rest of the Bloodline books, I've heard that The Legendary is the worst of them, with not many sensible ideas...</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to pick up Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies. It is a dynamic Blood Sorcery system for Vampire.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/105095.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\"> Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies - Onyx Path Publishing | Vampire: The Requiem | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies - God doesn't love me. But He's given me these teeth&nbsp;to spill your blood and these words to speak over your remains.&nbsp;And </div> </div> </div><br /> Reminds Me I need a copy for my 2.0 port.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T17:30:37-07:00","id":651949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie#post649866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello!<br /> <br /> I have Vampire: the Requiem book at home, but I have yet to play or GM it. Nevertheless, I tried considered both - and there are two questions that I struggle with:<br /> <br /> 1. When coming up with possible characters, I started to wonder: why would anyone actually decide to become a vampire? I mean... being vampire obviously sucks, because you have to literally prey on human beings. Wouldn't that turn almost anyone off the idea of allowing themselves to be Embraced? It would seem to me that only complete psychopaths and very desperate people would be willing to become vampires... How do you have your characters rationalize it, then?<br /> <br /> 2. When I was considering GM this game, I realized that I... have no idea what Vampire games could actually be about. It's a very rich setting, but what stories can you actually tell in it? Could you share any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not everybody is offered the embrace freely, some people get jumped one night and have it forced upon them. I mean honestly, do you think the Nosferatu would have any population at all if they relied on voluntary recruits? There are also those who spend a period as Ghouls before getting embraced and by then they're too indoctrinated or addicted to turn down the offer. Originally you had to get permission from the domain's ruler to embrace somebody, but it appears under the new rule systems, that is no longer the case. You can embrace whenever you want for whatever reason you want, but once you do so, they become your responsibility. If your childer misbehaves while still under your mentorship, you're the one who pays the price, so typically a sire will do a bit of research before embracing somebody.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=650645#post650645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the covenant books? I admit they would be my first choice, as the covenant descriptions in the core rulebook are really brief (for once, it's not actually explained what Lancea Sanctum's religion really is...).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum believe vampires exist to fulfill Satan's role in God's plan. In the actual bible, Satan and Lucifer are two very different beings. Satan means The Adversary and he actually works for God. His job is to test people's faith and punish those who abandon God's teachings. According to the Lancea Sanctum, It became increasingly difficult to fulfill his role as humanity grew in population, so they have devoted themselves to picking up the slack.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum defends the pious and the innocent with righteous fury, while punishing those who fall prey to sin and corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-04-2015, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T17:38:08-07:00","id":651951,"title":"","content":"As for a setting, the usual story is one of politics, each of the factions are vying against each other for land and privileges, sometimes doing so fairly and other times in a much more cutthroat fashion. You could also have a game centered around religion via a war between the Lancea Sanctum and the Circle of the Crone, or a dispute about ancient tradition and new age progression by pitting the Invictus against the Carthians.<br /> <br /> <br /> You could also do a sandbox mode via Unaligned in which the players hold no allegiance to anyone but themselves and are free to decide who they help or hinder. This, however, can be dangerous as the players run the risk of stepping outside of your planned story line.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> And then there is always the favorite idea that the rule book is just a general guideline or example of how you can run the game. I've been told several times that if you want to, you're perfectly able to alter or completely remove certain features about the game. I believe Predator's Taint was often thrown out because the risk of going into a frenzy whenever you met a new vampire for the first time was really frustrating.<br /> <br /> <br /> I watched a live play session in which the ST completely threw out the Masquerade system and vampires were allowed to walk around in the sun because somebody went back in time and performed some kind of massive ritual. The result was a game in which vampires lived openly among the humans as recognized citizens. Of course there were various social groups who didn't approve of their existence, and the government had specially designed law enforcement to deal with vampire criminals, but it was still an interesting setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-04-2015, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T20:42:35-07:00","id":652058,"title":"","content":"Ha! Interesting setting, Nyrufa <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, I have two requests for you, guys:<br /> <br /> 1. Could you share some specific examples of how the Embrace went for some your characters / NPCs? I still have trouble picturing it...<br /> <br /> 2. Could you tell me more of what role a vampire's clan can play in the game? Not in the sense of powers and weaknesses, but in the social / political sense. I mean, it's the covenants that are supposed to be political organisations, but the core rulebook also mentions clan elders etc. influencing their &quot;family&quot;... To what extent does something like that happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T23:13:12-07:00","id":652146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=652058#post652058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ha! Interesting setting, Nyrufa <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, I have two requests for you, guys:<br /> <br /> 1. Could you share some specific examples of how the Embrace went for some your characters / NPCs? I still have trouble picturing it...<br /> <br /> 2. Could you tell me more of what role a vampire's clan can play in the game? Not in the sense of powers and weaknesses, but in the social / political sense. I mean, it's the covenants that are supposed to be political organisations, but the core rulebook also mentions clan elders etc. influencing their &quot;family&quot;... To what extent does something like that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By the way, I know how you feel. I only own the first edition book too because I didn't know 2nd edition had come out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Well going by the core rule book (I don't have any of the extended material because I'm poor), the 5 clans would be appropriate for the following roles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mekhet</b> = Agents and Scholars. They prefer to hide in the dark and gather knowledge both occult and mundane.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu</b> = Spies and Enforcers. They distance themselves from society, but remain well informed and monstrously strong when threatened.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel</b> = Warriors and Investigators. Savages with amazing survival instincts, they make good trackers and are brutal in close quarters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Daeva</b> = Socialites and Campaign managers. They know how to twist people's emotions so they can't help but faun over every word they say. This (if done correctly) can actually make them even more powerful than the Ventrue, since their slaves are fooled into thinking it's their own free will to follow them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue</b> = Leaders and Business Associates. Any Ventrue who's not on top of the game and shows no signs of wanting it deserves a stake through the chest.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Most Likely Covenants:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone = Mekhet, Gangrel, Daeva. They're devoted to ancient pagan gods and goddesses, practicing rituals believed to have died out centuries ago.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lancea Sanctum = Nosferatu, Mekhet, Ventrue. Following a vampiric interpretation of the bible, they seek to fulfill Satan's role in God's plan, punishing the sinful and safeguarding the innocent.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul = Mekhet, Ventrue, Daeva. They seek to transcend the weaknesses of the vampire condition, they care not for politics but rather for if a student displays a willingness and capacity to learn.<br /> <br /> <br /> Invictus = Daeva, Ventrue, Nosferatu. The new Camarilla, the covenant was created by the elders, for the elders and the neonates can go fuck themselves. It also strongly upholds the traditions and laws of the masquerade to ensure its own survival.<br /> <br /> <br /> Carthian Movement = Any Clan. The new Anarchs, the covenant is much more organized than its original counterpart. They seek to bring about modern social reforms to the archaic society of the vampires, such as the belief that all should possess equal rights and privileges regardless of age or power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-05-2015, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:00:43-07:00","id":653045,"title":"","content":"Thanks, this is useful!<br /> <br /> So... I re-read the Ventrue book today. It was... a bit underwhelming for me, really. Too little of solid facts on Ventrue history, way too much space spent on Anneas and too many of vignettes. Overall, the book fleshes out the clan somewhat, but I can't help feeling that it could've been something better...<br /> <br /> I admit that I was very keen on picking up the clan books, as some of them (like Mekhet or Daeva) are a bit of mystery for me. But if the rest of the books were done in the same format, I fear my questions won't be answered in a satisfying way...<br /> <br /> BTW. One thing I noticed in the Ventrue book is that this clan seems really political... almost as if there were a covenant in itself. Do clans really hold that much power over individual members?<br /> <br /> BTW 2. The one thing I got from this book was that all Ventrue are... lordly and gravitate toward leadership. Why do you it's that way? Is it a cultural thing, or does Ventrue blood impose some sort of general personality on each of them?<br /> <br /> BTW 3. The interesting thing in the book are the mentions of non-vampire supernatural threats. So, vampires vs. other supernatural happenings is a valid chronicle choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:14:48-07:00","id":653048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=653045#post653045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW. One thing I noticed in the Ventrue book is that this clan seems really political... almost as if there were a covenant in itself. Do clans really hold that much power over individual members?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be. Some domains might not have any covenants at all and just be ruled by clans. But since it's a clan book it places its emphasis on the clan itself. Outside of the mechanics, there are few absolutes for the setting, so asking questions like these and some of the others, you have seen by now, the answer is almost always that 'it depends' on the Storyteller running things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW 2. The one thing I got from this book was that all Ventrue are... lordly and gravitate toward leadership. Why do you it's that way? Is it a cultural thing, or does Ventrue blood impose some sort of general personality on each of them? </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's the blood. Their clan discipline is dominance. Whether or not they're a leader they will try to impose themselves on others in a dominating fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW 3. The interesting thing in the book are the mentions of non-vampire supernatural threats. So, vampires vs. other supernatural happenings is a valid chronicle choice? </div> </div> </div>Of course, in my last vampire game werewolves were a big political enigma and the players managed to sway opinion regarding them and what to do with them. In the current werewolf game I'm playing there's werewolf on vampire aggression, and in the werewolf game I'm running, set in the same city as the vampire one, the werewolves are organizing and deciding whether or not they agree with how vampires are doing things. It's not something you have to do, but it's something you can. I like werewolves so I tend to put them in other games.<br /> <br /> I think the Gangrel, Mekhet and Nosferatu clan books are the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-05-2015, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T16:02:42-07:00","id":653120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=653045#post653045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, this is useful!<br /> <br /> So... I re-read the Ventrue book today. It was... a bit underwhelming for me, really. Too little of solid facts on Ventrue history, way too much space spent on Anneas and too many of vignettes. Overall, the book fleshes out the clan somewhat, but I can't help feeling that it could've been something better...<br /> <br /> I admit that I was very keen on picking up the clan books, as some of them (like Mekhet or Daeva) are a bit of mystery for me. But if the rest of the books were done in the same format, I fear my questions won't be answered in a satisfying way...<br /> <br /> BTW. One thing I noticed in the Ventrue book is that this clan seems really political... almost as if there were a covenant in itself. Do clans really hold that much power over individual members?<br /> <br /> BTW 2. The one thing I got from this book was that all Ventrue are... lordly and gravitate toward leadership. Why do you it's that way? Is it a cultural thing, or does Ventrue blood impose some sort of general personality on each of them?<br /> <br /> BTW 3. The interesting thing in the book are the mentions of non-vampire supernatural threats. So, vampires vs. other supernatural happenings is a valid chronicle choice?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the Requiem setting, each of the 5 clans embodies one aspect of the vampire mythos.<br /> <br /> <br /> Gangrel = Bestial and savage. Dusk to Dawn or Fright Night are good examples.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu = Hideous and terrifying. Think I am Legend or Blood + and you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Daeva = Seductive and charismatic. You don't need to look hard to find examples of them in today's media.<br /> <br /> Mekhet = Shadowy and graceful. It's hard to think of a popular comparison for them, but they like to manipulate events from behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> Ventrue = Powerful and overbearing. Count Dracula, or Victor (Underworld) are good examples of a Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> And yeah, it's very valid chronicle choice. Each of the games can take place in its own separate world or you can mix them all together, it's up to the ST's choice and what you plan to include in the story. Heck, you can even have a mixed party in which some players are Vampires and some are say mages or werewolves!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T20:07:03-07:00","id":653431,"title":"","content":"Since everyone else is recommending books, I'll weigh in:<br /> <br /> I prefer just using the core book. I'll probably get the 2e supplements as they come out, but for now I'm blissfully enjoying not having to deal with the supplement/merit/bloodline bloat that tends to happen with RPGs towards the end of their run.<br /> <br /> You may be happier just sticking with the 2e book(s) and improvising anything else you need. The books were only ever meant to be an example, anyway. Things like Domains and Covenants are described as running very differently city to city, region to region. Easy to get stuck in a rut of ideas you don't necessarily even like if you have the books right there telling you how it is.<br /> <br /> Plus some of 2e seems to contradict 1e fluff, and it can be a mess sorting out which is which edition.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's my recommendation. Everyone else gave great suggestions if you do want books in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:51:42-07:00","id":653497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=653431#post653431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The books were only ever meant to be an example, anyway. Things like Domains and Covenants are described as running very differently city to city, region to region. Easy to get stuck in a rut of ideas you don't necessarily even like if you have the books right there telling you how it is.<br /> <br /> Plus some of 2e seems to contradict 1e fluff, and it can be a mess sorting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like I said, the ST is apparently free to alter or rewrite setting material as they see fit. And the 2nd Edition overhauls the whole game. For one thing including touchstones which were not in 1ed, and it removes the concept of Golconda. 1st ed and 2nd ed are two different settings and rule systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T22:09:52-07:00","id":653508,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that Golconda's -removed-, per se, only that it didn't warrant wordcount in a book already stuffed to the gills. In general I tend to favor the approach that the fluff that's not contradicted is at least recommended if not outright still canon. YMMV, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T06:12:08-07:00","id":653787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=653508#post653508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that Golconda's -removed-, per se, only that it didn't warrant wordcount in a book already stuffed to the gills. In general I tend to favor the approach that the fluff that's not contradicted is at least recommended if not outright still canon. YMMV, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read a quick reference tat sounded like golconda. But I don't think they used that word.<br /> I need to read the social manuvering rules. The didn't click with me the first time.<br /> Char where is your galloi writup?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:10:27-07:00","id":654419,"title":"","content":"Re: Mekhet - see, my problem with them is that I can't find any fictional examples of a vampire like that. So, I'm not sure what they are supposed to be, really...<br /> <br /> Re: vampires vs other supernaturals - crossover games are one thing, but I was thinking of something a little different: vampires encountering really weird stuff, supernatural mysteries, Lovecraftian monsters / gods etc. There are mentions of such happenings in the Ventrue book - the &quot;Briareos&quot; being, or that doomed expedition to New Orleans that was driven mad by &quot;hags&quot;...<br /> <br /> On another note: Is Immortal Sinners worth reading? I have Wicked Dead and it's quite good (hey, the book even has the penanggalan!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:21:47-07:00","id":654425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=653787#post653787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Char where is your galloi writup?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/571810-converting-favorite-bloodlines-to-2nd-edition?p=574669#post574669\">Here.</a><br /> <br /> Any of my vampire homebrew that I share I put on the Homebrew Hub thread. I think Pendragon filed this one under Disciplines and Devotions instead of Bloodlines because that makes up the bulk of the writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-06-2015, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:08:48-07:00","id":654479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=654419#post654419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Mekhet - see, my problem with them is that I can't find any fictional examples of a vampire like that. So, I'm not sure what they are supposed to be, really...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well I'm not sure how to put it into words, but I'll try to clarify as best I can. Mekhet embody the aspect of vampire grace and elegance. The Mekhet are perfectionists who devote themselves to their craft. I believe the core book gives some examples of them, stating that a bodyguard is more likely to know an ornate fighting style instead of just being a bruiser with a club or sidearm. A scholar uses his centuries of unlife to acquire a vast wealth of knowledge, most of which he's probably committed to memory.<br /> <br /> When you see a depiction of a vampire dispatching a gang of enemies in the blink of an eye or nimbly weaving their way through heavy machine gun fire, chances are they're imitating a Mekhet. The Mekhet do not like being out in the open unless the have no other options, so when they perform a job, they do so cleanly and efficiently. Leaving behind as little a mess to clean up as possible. Once the job is finished, they retreat into the shadows for which they are named, vanishing without a trace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-06-2015, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:39:30-07:00","id":654494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=654419#post654419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Mekhet - see, my problem with them is that I can't find any fictional examples of a vampire like that. So, I'm not sure what they are supposed to be, really...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good at not getting caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T18:51:16-07:00","id":654636,"title":"","content":"There was a scene in an otherwise forgettable vampire movie where vamp was on a bus with a woman he was trying to seduce. He had a rose.<br /> Some mouthie punk came along started something. Said something to effect of &quot;what ya going to do hit me with the rose?&quot;<br /> The Vampire flicked into his eye stem first.<br /> I like to think he was a shadow.<br /> <br /> Mekhet are shadowy masterminds,. They are the investigators of things that dwell in the shadows. I see The original Nick Knight (Rick Springfield)or Mick st. John as Mekhet.<br /> The Mekhet are vampires of mystery and action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T19:32:46-07:00","id":654670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=654419#post654419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Mekhet - see, my problem with them is that I can't find any fictional examples of a vampire like that. So, I'm not sure what they are supposed to be, really...</div> </div> </div> </div>Lords are lordly. Savages are savage. Shadows are shadowy.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet, more than any other clan, are shadows of what they were in life. They're hollow, faded, in some way incomplete. They're missing something, something hard to define, but whose importance can be seen in its lacking. They don't work right, and they can't always tell what is or isn't off about themselves. The Daeva may be living dead, but the Mekhet are merely walking dead.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet hide not because they are fearful, but because they're so quiet and still that there's nothing to express. They're the man in the room who's so unremarkable and quiet that you forget he was there the whole time, listening. They watch, because others' lives are fuller than their own. The entire world around them is vastly richer than themselves by contrast. They read omens in the world. They listen. They go looking. They stalk. They obsess. And as they gather information, they become figures of mystique and power to the world around them, made rich and bold by their elusiveness. The rest of the world can't see that the mystique is a facade, skin-deep. There's nothing there as important as what we imagine there to be in the darkness. Ambitious Mekhet recognize that knowledge is a great weapon, but mystery is the greatest.<br /> <br /> There's an old man in the neighborhood who owns a rich and spooky manor. He hardly ever comes out. Some say he never does, that he hasn't been seen in the light since the fifties. Others claim to have seen him or talked to him, once or twice. Sometimes he writes a letter to the editor in the local paper. All manner of rumors surround the estate. Cats have gone missing. Now a child, too. His power is greater for how little they know about him, how much they wonder without ever seeing him. He's a Shadow.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet is the apprentice whom you don't recognize as significant until he stabs the villain in the back and usurps his place. He's the faceless authority in dimly-lit video messages who doesn't seem to have any identity outside of his directions, because his everyday life is so innocuous. He's the enforcer whose capabilities are unknown because nobody ever witnesses what is presumably his work. He's the vampire who seems introspective and sympathetic at first, who seems cautious that something has changed for the worse in him, until you realize just how broken he is, and how those he loves suffer worse than those he hates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=654419#post654419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: vampires vs other supernaturals - crossover games are one thing, but I was thinking of something a little different: vampires encountering really weird stuff, supernatural mysteries, Lovecraftian monsters / gods etc. There are mentions of such happenings in the Ventrue book - the &quot;Briareos&quot; being, or that doomed expedition to New Orleans that was driven mad by &quot;hags&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's absolutely something you can do with Requiem, for which the Mekhet, the Ordo Dracul and the Circle of the Crone are especially well suited. It's not necessarily a core focus the way it is in, say, Mage: the Awakening, but it's definitely something described in the world of Requiem, and it's not uncommon for a domain to fail to recognize an outside context problem until it becomes the most pressing issue around which the domain revolves. Wicked Dead, of course, covers some phenomena like that as you saw, and the other clanbooks continue to hint at bizarre mysteries beyond the Kindred. I think you would very much like the end of the Mekhet story and the terrifying uncertainty it engenders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T19:56:16-07:00","id":654681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=654419#post654419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Mekhet - see, my problem with them is that I can't find any fictional examples of a vampire like that. So, I'm not sure what they are supposed to be, really...</div> </div> </div> </div>There are very few pop culture examples of Mekhet. This is at least in part because they're all about seeing while remaining unseen, so any good example would by definition be difficult to pinpoint. I haven't seen it, but I've heard Adam and Eve from <i>Last Lovers Left Alive</i> are pretty good examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T20:27:17-07:00","id":654724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=654419#post654419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Mekhet - see, my problem with them is that I can't find any fictional examples of a vampire like that. So, I'm not sure what they are supposed to be, really...</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the wamphyri fit the bill, particularly Nephran Malinari and Lord Szwart of the later trilogy, though they would be high Blood Potency unique bloodline mekhet. Of course you might have not read that. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486089-which-pop-culture-vampire-belongs-to-which-clan\">This</a> thread might help, where we were matching fictional vampires to clans, though even then finding mekhet was difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Re: vampires vs other supernaturals - crossover games are one thing, but I was thinking of something a little different: vampires encountering really weird stuff, supernatural mysteries, Lovecraftian monsters / gods etc. There are mentions of such happenings in the Ventrue book - the &quot;Briareos&quot; being, or that doomed expedition to New Orleans that was driven mad by &quot;hags&quot;... </div> </div> </div>Nothing keeps vampires from encountering the weirder stuff in the World of Darkness. Some of the VII factions were created explicitly because of that, and one of the novels, Silent Knife, was about <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">vampires that had found a Very Weird Thing and were taking advantage of it until it took advantage of them.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note: Is Immortal Sinners worth reading? I have Wicked Dead and it's quite good (hey, the book even has the penanggalan!). </div> </div> </div>I like it more than Wicked Dead, but tastes may vary. Immortal Sinners and most of the other Night Horrors books tend to focus on NPCs. So while the Wicked Dead focuses on types of proto-vampires and vampire variants like the draugr, Immortal Sinners will show you actual vampires with a few pages about them. A cpuple of them are even vampires who have run into weird stuff, or vampires who are weird stuff. Also a few examples of mekhet, like Eddie Vines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-06-2015, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T06:52:52-07:00","id":655072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=654419#post654419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Mekhet - see, my problem with them is that I can't find any fictional examples of a vampire like that. So, I'm not sure what they are supposed to be, really...</div> </div> </div> </div>Bill Compton in the Southern Vampire Mysteries would be a possible example. He's a typical power climbing asshole but what makes him special is his memory for details and the fact that he quietly accumulated extensive personal information on every vampire in North America and he'll sell it to any vampire who'll pay him for it.<br /> You aren't going to find a lot of pop culture references to fit the Mekhet archetype because they are the supporting characters who do the fill in the blank work for the main characters and don't get a lot of attention for it. And vampires don't usually occupy tertiary roles in the entertainment media, they are the primary character, or they are the secondary characters who are very important to the main character for x reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T17:53:10-07:00","id":657215,"title":"","content":"Again, thanks for all of the replies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you don't mind, I have a request: all of you have surely created many characters, either as players or as GMs. Could you, then, share some more examples of how people get Embraced? I still have trouble picturing the possible circumstances....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T21:45:36-07:00","id":657378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=657215#post657215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, thanks for all of the replies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you don't mind, I have a request: all of you have surely created many characters, either as players or as GMs. Could you, then, share some more examples of how people get Embraced? I still have trouble picturing the possible circumstances....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Actually I've never played the game. Like, at all. I don't know any place / people around where I live who play it. Kind of ironic since I live in Georgia, where I think the creators of WoD live. Not entirely sure about that.<br /> <br /> The general reason for why somebody is embraced again falls upon the sire. Usually the sire believes there is something about the individual that warrants the embrace. Nobody just walks up to a vampire and asks to be turned (unless they're a ghoul), remember that vampires try to make it a point that humans don't know they exist. They might possess a certain set of skills or talents, or perhaps the have valuable contacts and resources the sire wishes to take advantage of. However there are also cases in which the sire embraces a mortal as a form of punishment. Both the Nosferatu and the Lancea Sanctum are notorious for this, with the Nosferatu targeting others for their vanity and the Lancea Sanctum targeting others for their sinful behavior.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-09-2015, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T22:35:08-07:00","id":657414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=657215#post657215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, thanks for all of the replies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you don't mind, I have a request: all of you have surely created many characters, either as players or as GMs. Could you, then, share some more examples of how people get Embraced? I still have trouble picturing the possible circumstances....</div> </div> </div> </div>You should check out <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/87335/Scenes-of-the-Embrace?term=scenes+of+the+embrace\" target=\"_blank\">Scenes of the Embrace</a>. 14 different embrace scenes, two themed after each of the 7 deadly sins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T05:19:19-07:00","id":657704,"title":"","content":"I ST vampire, I haven't gotten to play it, but among players and one or two NPCs that I can remember, vampires who sired distant family members to retain a connection with their family, a couple times vampires saved a dying person, not always to benefit the dying, once saving a nobleman who the vampire impressed with their ruthlessness, embracing an arms dealer with lots of connections to get control over some of said connections when ghouling her wouldn't work with her schedule, one ghoul who sawed open their regnant's chest and ate their heart, one ascended revenant resulted from a feeding gone overboard, a quintet Embraced in defiance of the Prince's law to seal an oath of conspiracy between vampire conspirators, one Embrace out of spite of a bloodline, an enemy keeping the childe from becoming a true 'part of the family,' and she ended up Embracing her son in further rebellion, a few to reward faithful ghouls, at least one act of love, and one child taken as part of a bargain with a member of the Ordo Dracul so the sire's bloodline could be studied without said vampire having to act as a lab rat.<br /> <br /> That run on sentence wounded me.<br /> <br /> There's dozens of examples throughout the books, as well. I believe in the Strix Fiction Anthology one person becomes a vampire by spending too much time looking in a mirror. <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/TheUnquietDead.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Here's</a> a fan supplement with 7 sample NPCs with brief information about some of their Embraces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-09-2015, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:51:33-07:00","id":667605,"title":"","content":"If you've got anymore questions, feel free to ask. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:09:25-07:00","id":667619,"title":"","content":"Right now, I've run out of questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I soooo want to play this game! I can't find a ST for a PbP game, though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:14:55-07:00","id":667622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=667619#post667619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, I've run out of questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I soooo want to play this game! I can't find a ST for a PbP game, though...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I had the same problem. Vampire is a very political themed game, so it's a bit harder to put together. You said you play 1st edition, right? Most players seem like they prefer 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:42:28-07:00","id":667642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie#post649866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello!<br /> <br /> I have Vampire: the Requiem book at home, but I have yet to play or GM it. Nevertheless, I tried considered both - and there are two questions that I struggle with:<br /> <br /> 1. When coming up with possible characters, I started to wonder: why would anyone actually decide to become a vampire? I mean... being vampire obviously sucks, because you have to literally prey on human beings. Wouldn't that turn almost anyone off the idea of allowing themselves to be Embraced? It would seem to me that only complete psychopaths and very desperate people would be willing to become vampires... How do you have your characters rationalize it, then?<br /> <br /> 2. When I was considering GM this game, I realized that I... have no idea what Vampire games could actually be about. It's a very rich setting, but what stories can you actually tell in it? Could you share any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding 1: Sometimes you don't decide it. Sometimes some immortal predator becomes obsessed with you for some reason. Check Dracula From Bran Stoker for example.<br /> <br /> Regarding 2: Loss of innocence, damnation, damned if you do - damned if you don't, ennui, the depression of realizing everything you've ever knew will, a thousand years from now, be dust - that moment broken by the searing thirst of a sensual moment more pleasurable than the best sex you've ever had. <br /> <br /> The list goes on and on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:55:12-07:00","id":667647,"title":"","content":"One word: denial.<br /> Given how much Hollywood has romanticized vampires do you honestly believe your average person wouldn't jump at the chance to live out their Twilight dreams? It is also possible to deny that you will do harm, after all killing isn't a necessary part of feeding.<br /> There will also be those for whom the idea of living at the expense of others isn't that hard to accept and may already be a part of their lives. Hardened criminals, the hate filled, people who really don't empathize with strangers or the faceless masses. The CWOD example of Montrovant, the Dark One, is a crusader who was turned after he became disillusioned by fighting in the holy land. This was also the idea behind Nicholas Knight in the TV show Forever Knight. Is it that hard to imagine someone who grew up in a violent neighborhood might choose to join a gang that drinks blood?\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T18:13:07-07:00","id":667681,"title":"","content":"People have done as bad or worse things in pursuit of a myriad of different things. Mix in a mystical substance that's more addictive than drugs and better than sex AND is a guaranteed shot at not dying of old age...yeah, I wouldn't be surprised at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T18:25:42-07:00","id":667685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=667647#post667647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One word: denial.<br /> Given how much Hollywood has romanticized vampires do you honestly believe your average person wouldn't jump at the chance to live out their Twilight dreams? It is also possible to deny that you will do harm, after all killing isn't a necessary part of feeding.<br /> There will also be those for whom the idea of living at the expense of others isn't that hard to accept and may already be a part of their lives. Hardened criminals, the hate filled, people who really don't empathize with strangers or the faceless masses. The CWOD example of Montrovant, the Dark One, is a crusader who was turned after he became disillusioned by fighting in the holy land. This was also the idea behind Nicholas Knight in the TV show Forever Knight. Is it that hard to imagine someone who grew up in a violent neighborhood might choose to join a gang that drinks blood?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. Back in the old days, monsters were stories parents used to scare children into behaving, but in the modern day they have been romanticized in more ways than one. The people of today glorify and admire the creatures that encouraged their ancestors to lock their doors and sleep with a weapon under the pillow. It would not be difficult for a vampire to pluck some random fool off the street with offers of power and status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T21:57:59-07:00","id":667818,"title":"","content":"Varsovian in terms of Embrace stories that are mine and from friends.<br /> <br /> Dragon Gangrel: Circa 70s turkey, 10 yr old girl was taken from an orphanage and raised in the mansion of a Wyrm Prince (Dragon who is a Prince) and grew up as mansion staff/herd/lab assistant/goffer. At age 19 she was fatally drained because someone attempting a new coil failed and their Beast seized control. Before she died she was found by one of the Dragons on the premise and Embraced. The rational was she had been considered an adequate servant in life, was well versed with the Ordo and because with Final Death of the failed Dragon there was an opening and they decided, why not her?<br /> <br /> Unaligned Daeva: 1870s, wild west; a Daeva ran across a very beautiful woman who ran a saloon and also happened to be really good with a pistol. The daeve was smitten with her because she had a powerful personality, was beautiful, was dangerous (by kine standards) and was smart. To the Sire the woman was a perfect candidate for Embrace (and she was totally crushing on her) and embraced her. As I recall she blew her Sire's head off with a coach gun several months after Embrace while the Sire was mid-coitus with a man they had picked up together. Had &quot;Payback&quot; engraved in butt of the gun afterward.<br /> <br /> Unaligned Ventrue: 13th Century Mongol Empire, the son of a minor mongol chief who had been seriously wounded in battle during an early raid into Persia. Laying on field at night waiting to die, two Vampires appeared above him and offered him a deal. He could accept the Embrace, become a vampire and continue to rape and pillage with them in the name of the Mongols (they were mongols too) or they'd drink what little blood he had left and leave his corpse for the crows. He choose the Embrace. He joined their cotiere whose gig was to go into cities and recruit Kindred to the Mongol cause and if they resisted, sabotage defenses/troops/food stores to make it easier for the Mongols to take cities. (it was a pretty fun game of spycraft as it turned out).<br /> <br /> Carthian Revenant: Victorian England, was attacked by what he believed to a Nosferatu, drained and dropped in a bog. Sank into the muck before day-light and then rose the next time. Bit of a pyromaniac socialist that one turned out to be.<br /> <br /> Pre-cursor Crone Mekhet: was a priest to in Set Cult in late Bronze Age Egypt. The cult was a front to a large coterie/cult of Mekhet. He was the ghoul/personal assistant to one of the Mekhet. When ghouls appeared in the middle of the day to kill the sleeping coterie, the priest drove them off with Cruac which he had been secretly learning to impress his Master. His master was shocked and quickly Embraced him as a reward for defending his masters and for learning blood magic. Turns out vamps don't like the idea of their human pets wielding blood magic. Went on to be a pretty scary blood sorcerer, helped drive off the Sea People invading Egypt.<br /> <br /> Invictus Nosferatu: He had been a soldier turned in WWI. He had been caught in one of the earl poison gas attacks before they had masks. Two Nos feeding on the fatally wounded came across him gagging and gasping in no-mans-land and made a bet. There was a rumor going around at the time chemical weapons first appeared in the war that you couldn't embrace victims of them. One bet the other 5 Franks that he couldn't embrace the soldier. He was subsequently embraced and his Sire won the 5 Franks. He was almost killed near the end of the war because he went feeding in a trench and got caught in an arillary bombardment. Two of his coterie-mates got taken out in one round of combat/shelling.<br /> <br /> I play with a lot of history buffs in case you notice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:43:32-07:00","id":668078,"title":"","content":"You <i>do</i> have wild talents <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Those are all pretty good character concepts and embrace stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T10:28:37-07:00","id":669844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>youvegotwildtalents</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=667818#post667818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unaligned Ventrue: 13th Century Mongol Empire, the son of a minor mongol chief who had been seriously wounded in battle during an early raid into Persia. Laying on field at night waiting to die, two Vampires appeared above him and offered him a deal. He could accept the Embrace, become a vampire and continue to rape and pillage with them in the name of the Mongols (they were mongols too) or they'd drink what little blood he had left and leave his corpse for the crows. He choose the Embrace. He joined their cotiere whose gig was to go into cities and recruit Kindred to the Mongol cause and if they resisted, sabotage defenses/troops/food stores to make it easier for the Mongols to take cities. (it was a pretty fun game of spycraft as it turned out).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is amazing and needs to be a Dark Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:23:39-07:00","id":671020,"title":"","content":"Okay! I was re-reading the core Requiem book and I have some more questions:<br /> <br /> 1. The book is says that the vampires don't mature personality-wise after the Embrace. Sooo.. does it mean that a vampire that was 20 when Embraced is going to behave like an impetous, naive 20 year old forever? Even when he's 500 years old?<br /> <br /> 2. You guys mentioned that vampires often Embrace ghouls. But the ghouls are all, by their nature, subject to Vinculum. Does it mean that, after their Embrace, such new vampires are blood-bound, too?<br /> <br /> 3. By the way, the First Tradition says that a vampire shouldn't reveal himself to mortals and that vampires that do so should be put to death. So, why is the practice of creating ghouls allowed? It is a breach of Masquerade, too...<br /> <br /> 4. Speaking of Traditions: the Second Tradition forbids the creation of new vampires. Still, obviously, it keeps happening. Sooo... it's a Tradition that nobody pays attention to, right?<br /> <br /> 5. And speaking of Embracing: it is said the sires are responsible for the tutelage of their childe. But... why would any childe listen to his sire? Let's say you are Embraced and turned into a monster against your will - would you really be interested in listening to the monster that did that to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:37:05-07:00","id":671033,"title":"","content":"1 - Not exactly, it's more like vampires don't adapt well to changes in society as the ages pass by. Nobody likes the idea that the way they were brought up is considered outdated and the times are changing. It's like grandparents having trouble using smart phones and computers. Elder vampires who grew up in a time where you sent messages on hand written parchment and delivered by carrier pigeon still feel uncomfortable using electronic mail or phone calls. Such Elders often use Ghouls, or embrace younger childer in order to act as proxies for keeping in touch with the modern times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - Actually, I would like to know that too. Never thought to ask for confirmation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3 - The tradition applies to revealing yourself to mortals and then letting them go free. It's okay for a vampire to slip up once in a while as long as they cover up their mistakes. This typically means one of four things; Give the witness a memory wipe, enslave them, embrace them, or kill them.<br /> <br /> <br /> 4 - The actual terms of the second tradition mean you can't embrace somebody <i>without permission</i> and the actual purpose of this tradition is so that the leaders of the domain have knowledge on all the vampires operating within their territory, even newly created ones. This rule seems to have been thrown out in 2nd edition where you're free to embrace as you please, but you take full responsibility for their actions as long as they remain under your tutelage. Besides, if vampires were forbidden to create more of their own, they would have died out centuries ago during the time of the crusades.<br /> <br /> <br /> 5 - You have a point that, yes, a childe is under no obligation to learn from their sire, but you should keep in mind that once they are released, they are wholly responsible for their own actions. Nobody is going to hold their hand and walk them through the night like their Sire tried to do. If they make a mistake, they are the ones who get punished for it, not the one who made them, so even if you hate your sire, it is at least a good idea to learn what you can from them before striking out on your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-19-2015, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T10:12:21-07:00","id":671047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671020#post671020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay! I was re-reading the core Requiem book and I have some more questions:<br /> <br /> 1. The book is says that the vampires don't mature personality-wise after the Embrace. Sooo.. does it mean that a vampire that was 20 when Embraced is going to behave like an impetous, naive 20 year old forever? Even when he's 500 years old?</div> </div> </div> </div> To an extent. Naivity goes away with experience and knowledge. But he's likely to remain immature, even as he develops as an elder. Or course, that's entirely in 1e. 2nd edition has completely dropped the whole static-vampire thing. So its not really supported beyond the vampire core. I wouldn't put too much worry about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. You guys mentioned that vampires often Embrace ghouls. But the ghouls are all, by their nature, subject to Vinculum. Does it mean that, after their Embrace, such new vampires are blood-bound, too? </div> </div> </div> Its up to the ST, but generally yes. Many vampires blood bond their childer as a matter of course anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. By the way, the First Tradition says that a vampire shouldn't reveal himself to mortals and that vampires that do so should be put to death. So, why is the practice of creating ghouls allowed? It is a breach of Masquerade, too...<br /> <br /> 4. Speaking of Traditions: the Second Tradition forbids the creation of new vampires. Still, obviously, it keeps happening. Sooo... it's a Tradition that nobody pays attention to, right? </div> </div> </div> Vampires are naturally hypocrites. You're expected to break the law, but just not get caught doing it. Vampires pretty much break the Masquerade any time they feed, but they still feed. Ghouls are excused, because once they're a ghoul, they're part of the Blood. There's lots of self-justifications running around, and that's kind of the point. Childer aren't allowed, but it happens. Even in the Lancea, its a sin, but it happens, and there's public whipping, and then everyone goes home happy. Diablarie is forbidden... except when its allowed. Its the ultimate thrill, the ultimate drug for vampires, and they all secretly crave a taste.<br /> <br /> Its all about whatever excuses you can come up with for breaking the law, not just avoiding it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. And speaking of Embracing: it is said the sires are responsible for the tutelage of their childe. But... why would any childe listen to his sire? Let's say you are Embraced and turned into a monster against your will - would you really be interested in listening to the monster that did that to you? </div> </div> </div> One, who else you going to listen to? Just how do you plan on surviving without them? Or do you have convient access to blood and sunless rooms when you didn't plan on becoming a vampire? Sheer necessity here. Two, after a bit, Stockholm Syndrome sets in. Or there's Majesty, Dominate, the blood bond. Maybe you stick around for revenge. Three, not all Embraces are against the will; many go willingly to the fang. To be honest, for all the talk about how much being a vampire sucks, no pun intended? It certain as hell beats growing old and dying, your body betraying you, your memory failing. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T10:31:53-07:00","id":671058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671020#post671020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The book is says that the vampires don't mature personality-wise after the Embrace. Sooo.. does it mean that a vampire that was 20 when Embraced is going to behave like an impetous, naive 20 year old forever? Even when he's 500 years old?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those things that's kind of changed in the 10 years since the core book came out and the setting has grown. As Nyrufa said, it's not that they don't mature emotionally, it's just that they have a lot of difficulty adjusting to the rapidly changing times. And even that's been de-emphasized as of 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671020#post671020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. You guys mentioned that vampires often Embrace ghouls. But the ghouls are all, by their nature, subject to Vinculum. Does it mean that, after their Embrace, such new vampires are blood-bound, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Also, the embrace itself requires the subject to consume a point of the sire's Vitae, which would also prompt a roll to check for Vinculum. It's incredibly common for freshly-embraced childer to start out at least one stage of blood bond to their Sire, if not more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671020#post671020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. By the way, the First Tradition says that a vampire shouldn't reveal himself to mortals and that vampires that do so should be put to death. So, why is the practice of creating ghouls allowed? It is a breach of Masquerade, too...</div> </div> </div> </div>Different Domains interpret the Traditions in different ways, so in some cities, creating a Ghoul might very well be considered a breach of the First Tradition. More often though, ghouls don't really count, since by definition they are blood bound to their regnant and are therefore unlikely to reveal her identity to any mortals. Similarly, in some Domains it's considered perfectly fine for a vampire's Herds to know about her undead nature, as long as she compels them to keep it secret through some combination of blood bonds, Vitae addiction, and/or disciplines like Dominate and Majesty. And if some random mortal happens to catch you feeding or something? No problem, just erase his memory, or ghoul him, or kill him, or what ever you've got to do to plug the leak. As long as you patch up your own Masquerade breaches, no harm no foul. Others will not be so forgiving, just depends on the local political climate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671020#post671020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Speaking of Traditions: the Second Tradition forbids the creation of new vampires. Still, obviously, it keeps happening. Sooo... it's a Tradition that nobody pays attention to, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, different Domains will have different rules about when Embrace is or isn't allowed. Only the most starkly traditional Prince will completely forbid embrace under any circumstances within his city. Most often, Embracing is allowed, but only with permission from the Prince himself (or maybe he delegates that duty to someone else), and some cities will be more or less discerning with granting permission. Some very liberal Princes might prefer that Sires ask forgiveness rather than permission.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671020#post671020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. And speaking of Embracing: it is said the sires are responsible for the tutelage of their childe. But... why would any childe listen to his sire? Let's say you are Embraced and turned into a monster against your will - would you really be interested in listening to the monster that did that to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember the part about most Childer starting out at least one stage blood bound to their Sire? This is why. It's extremely common for Sires to keep their Childer bound to their will through blood bonds and/or Discipline use for the first few years or decades of the Childe's unlife, until they've proven they can take care of themselves. A neonate has to <i>earn</i> her right to free will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-19-2015, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T12:40:43-07:00","id":671206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671020#post671020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. You guys mentioned that vampires often Embrace ghouls. But the ghouls are all, by their nature, subject to Vinculum. Does it mean that, after their Embrace, such new vampires are blood-bound, too?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that one is answered in the FAQ.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the Embrace cause blood bonds or blood addiction?<br /> No. </div> </div> </div>I guess in that one instance all the power goes into raising the childe from the dead and establishing blood sympathy. If you think about it, that's sort of like a blood bond anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:39:57-07:00","id":671256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671206#post671206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that one is answered in the FAQ.<br /> <br /> I guess in that one instance all the power goes into raising the childe from the dead and establishing blood sympathy. If you think about it, that's sort of like a blood bond anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was explained that way in the 1E rulebook, too. But I was wondering about something else: a ghoul is *already* blood-bound. If he / she gets Embraced, does the blood bond go away or persist in the ghoul's vampire existence?<br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <br /> Thanks for the answers. So, you guys say that the idea of psychologically-static vampires was done away with? Is there a specific book that explored that matter? I admit that I don't like this idea very much, as it might suggest that vampires can't evolve as people, which would limit the RP possibilities. Also, I like the idea of the elder vampire being these scary predators that are, in a way, wise - even if they *look* young.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I do like the core rulebook's idea that vampires are somewhat &quot;dead inside&quot;. Was this done away with, too?<br /> <br /> I also have another question: how long does a childe's tutelage last, on average? Also, are the PCs supposed to be childer who have already been released by their sires? Finally, when is a newly-created vampire supposed to meet the city's Prince - immediately after being Embraced, or when they are being released?<br /> <br /> BTW. An observation: Requiem is a game that seems to require a lot of planning. I mean, a Mage: the Awakening game can be a simple adventure with mages investigating some strange happenings etc. But in Requiem, you really need to plan things before you begin to GM - the politics seem central to this game, so you need to come up with a whole power structure for a city before you start anything...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:47:43-07:00","id":671270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671256#post671256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW. An observation: Requiem is a game that seems to require a lot of planning. I mean, a Mage: the Awakening game can be a simple adventure with mages investigating some strange happenings etc. But in Requiem, you really need to plan things before you begin to GM - the politics seem central to this game, so you need to come up with a whole power structure for a city before you start anything...</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, the politics can be thrown out if you want. There are nomadic games and as mentioned, cities without covenants or real organization, and even in a game with a lush political setting the game is not always going to be about becoming Prince. But at the core, the game just like vampires themselves is a social thing. One of the best pieces of advice I ever got for vampire was to just make a list of characters. You don't have to have a fully written-up character sheet for each, just a name, clan and covenant and a sentence or two about them. That way you always have someone the players can engage with. I've since added some things to it, essentially noting 'Things They Want' and 'Things They Can Do.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T14:09:34-07:00","id":671297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671256#post671256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, I do like the core rulebook's idea that vampires are somewhat &quot;dead inside&quot;. Was this done away with, too?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much. As the setting got more and more established it made less and less sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T14:23:46-07:00","id":671338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671270#post671270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really, the politics can be thrown out if you want. There are nomadic games and as mentioned, cities without covenants or real organization, and even in a game with a lush political setting the game is not always going to be about becoming Prince. But at the core, the game just like vampires themselves is a social thing. One of the best pieces of advice I ever got for vampire was to just make a list of characters. You don't have to have a fully written-up character sheet for each, just a name, clan and covenant and a sentence or two about them. That way you always have someone the players can engage with. I've since added some things to it, essentially noting 'Things They Want' and 'Things They Can Do.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Good advice! Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671297#post671297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, pretty much. As the setting got more and more established it made less and less sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... no more ennui of spiritually empty monsters? Are the Kindred supposed to be just like mortal people? Hmmmmmm. Not sure I like it. It removes one interested downside of being a vampire...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T14:34:03-07:00","id":671342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671256#post671256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was explained that way in the 1E rulebook, too. But I was wondering about something else: a ghoul is *already* blood-bound. If he / she gets Embraced, does the blood bond go away or persist in the ghoul's vampire existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they are still bound, but I'm not positive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671256#post671256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers. So, you guys say that the idea of psychologically-static vampires was done away with? Is there a specific book that explored that matter? I admit that I don't like this idea very much, as it might suggest that vampires can't evolve as people, which would limit the RP possibilities. Also, I like the idea of the elder vampire being these scary predators that are, in a way, wise - even if they *look* young.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I do like the core rulebook's idea that vampires are somewhat &quot;dead inside&quot;. Was this done away with, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;dead inside&quot; thing hasn't exactly gone away, but it has evolved a bit over time. The way I like to think of it, there's nothing about being a vampire that automatically makes you emotionless as soon as you're embraced. But, after spending a long enough time watching everything change as you stay exactly the same... After the people you knew and loved grow old and die, the values that were central to the society you lived in shift to the point where young neonates call your ideals backwards and draconian... you're naturally going to become quite jaded. So vampire's do tend to be emotionally deadened, but it's more a result of the process of Humanity slipping away, rather than an inherent part of the curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671256#post671256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have another question: how long does a childe's tutelage last, on average? Also, are the PCs supposed to be childer who have already been released by their sires? Finally, when is a newly-created vampire supposed to meet the city's Prince - immediately after being Embraced, or when they are being released?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of that depends. Some sires may throw their Childer into the world as soon as possible, others may try to keep their Childer as slaves for as long as they can get away with it. &quot;As the story demands&quot; is always a good rule of thumb. The default assumption for PCs fresh out of character creation is that they're at least experienced enough to join a Covenant, which probably means they've been released by their Sires, but they are still young enough that they cling to Humanity. I'd say no more than 100 or so years dead, since Blood Potency rises naturally at a rate of 1 dot every 50 years, and BP3 is the highest you can start at from base character creation. Of course, you can always change this default assumption if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671256#post671256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW. An observation: Requiem is a game that seems to require a lot of planning. I mean, a Mage: the Awakening game can be a simple adventure with mages investigating some strange happenings etc. But in Requiem, you really need to plan things before you begin to GM - the politics seem central to this game, so you need to come up with a whole power structure for a city before you start anything...</div> </div> </div> </div>Politics is a big part of the setting, but it doesn't have to be a focus of the story if you don't want it to be. I learned the game through LARP, so that colors my interpretation of the game - I'm used to heavily factionalized, PvP focused games. But thats only one style of play, there are a lot of other ways you can go with Requiem. A fun one for a group who hasn't played Vampire before is to have the PCs all get embraced together, but their Sire disappears or dies before getting a chance to teach them about what they are (or maybe she never intended to teach them in the first place) and now they've got to work it out themselves, as a group. If you want to throw a wrench in that, you can have the local vampires hunting them, trying to cover up the potential masquerade risk of a handful of neonates wandering around without any guidance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-19-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:01:43-07:00","id":671353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671338#post671338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... no more ennui of spiritually empty monsters? Are the Kindred supposed to be just like mortal people? Hmmmmmm. Not sure I like it. It removes one interested downside of being a vampire...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's still the berserker rages you fall into now and then. <br /> <br /> That's the thing, really, they were always supposed to be kind of emotionless - right until they flip out and tear your head off. It's not really internally consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:45:39-07:00","id":671379,"title":"","content":"On the Embrace and blood bonds, that's one thing I personally change in my games: whether through mysticism or through the sheer trauma of dying and rising from the grave, I rule that the Embrace shatters all previous blood bonds (and possibly other long lasting conditions). It's entirely possible for a sire to try to rebond his childe immediately, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T16:35:30-07:00","id":671471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671379#post671379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Embrace and blood bonds, that's one thing I personally change in my games: whether through mysticism or through the sheer trauma of dying and rising from the grave, I rule that the Embrace shatters all previous blood bonds (and possibly other long lasting conditions). It's entirely possible for a sire to try to rebond his childe immediately, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is how the rules read now as oppose to Masq.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T21:23:19-07:00","id":671664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=671338#post671338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So... no more ennui of spiritually empty monsters? Are the Kindred supposed to be just like mortal people? Hmmmmmm. Not sure I like it. It removes one interested downside of being a vampire...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampires at least try to maintain some resemblance of humanity. If they do not, they fall prey to their Beast, a force inside them that is concerned with its own survival and <b>nothing else.</b><br /> <br /> Pretty much all of the WoD games have a force whether internal or external that is there to prevent your character from going HAM with their powers and acting like, well, a monster. Vampires have the Beast, Werewolves have Harmony, Mages have Paradox and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:02:54-07:00","id":672156,"title":"","content":"Oh, I know about the Beast and Humanity... But I was referring to something else: the idea that the vampires lose something essential because of the Embrace, some piece of their soul that is capable of true love, artistic talent etc. It's mentioned in the core rulebook &quot;Fact vs Myth&quot; section. I wonder if this was retconned away later? I kind of like that...<br /> <br /> I have another question today: if I understand correctly, every new vampire only has minimum amount of Vitae immediately after the Embrace, right? So, if someone's Embrace happens shortly before dawn, then... such a character has smallchance of survival. Because such a character won't have many opportunities to feed before falling asleep... and then, he'd spend his remaining Vitae when waking up at sundown. So... immediate torpor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:21:51-07:00","id":672162,"title":"","content":"Probably, but a newly created vampire would be humanity 7 and blood potency 1 by definition, so the torpor would only last a week. Plus the sire could just feed them extra vitae when they rose to prevent that. Or do the same the next night instead, if they're BP 3 or higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:49:18-07:00","id":672209,"title":"","content":"I see. But if a vampire was abandoned immediately after their Embrace, they would be in trouble, right? I'm asking that, as I kind of like the story idea Charlaquin presented. I'm wondering about the complications that could befall such a totally abandoned coteries of new vampires, though - would they even manage to figure out they need to feed before falling into torpor..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:54:08-07:00","id":672214,"title":"","content":"Yes, yes they would. Fortunately the vampiric condition comes with an instruction manual that covers the basics. <br /> <br /> Now, what they would do with the corpse is another question entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T11:36:47-07:00","id":672253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672209#post672209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. But if a vampire was abandoned immediately after their Embrace, they would be in trouble, right? I'm asking that, as I kind of like the story idea Charlaquin presented. I'm wondering about the complications that could befall such a totally abandoned coteries of new vampires, though - would they even manage to figure out they need to feed before falling into torpor..?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely they would fall to Frenzy before that happened, and even if they dont know they need to feed on human blood, their Beasts sure do. Then you've got one or more bodies on your hands, which adds another potential complication, if the cops start investigating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T11:38:36-07:00","id":672254,"title":"","content":"I see. Okay, so here's a million dollar question: why just not turn yourself in? Wouldn't a typical, moral person do just that, if she found out that she's been infected with a &quot;disease&quot; that makes her a danger to other? I would do that, personally...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T11:48:12-07:00","id":672256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672156#post672156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I know about the Beast and Humanity... But I was referring to something else: the idea that the vampires lose something essential because of the Embrace, some piece of their soul that is capable of true love, artistic talent etc. It's mentioned in the core rulebook &quot;Fact vs Myth&quot; section. I wonder if this was retconned away later? I kind of like that...</div> </div> </div> </div>There never were any kind of mechanical bits to reinforce that, so it's not really so much removed as deemphasized. Later books still tend to portray vampires and their psychology as somewhat &quot;off&quot; in an unquantifiable way. The specific sense that vampires are muted and faded, only able to muster the memories of the emotions they had in life, isn't really brought up anymore, because a good number of people found that notion an obstacle to getting into the mood of the game \u2013 the idea kind of translates in some folks' heads to &quot;vampires are fake people who move on rote and are hard to relate to.&quot; The idea wasn't communicating well. Still, as I say, there is a sense that, whether by nature or nurture, you spend long enough in the Requiem, you're going to turn out somehow &quot;different,&quot; in some vaguely ominous way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672156#post672156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another question today: if I understand correctly, every new vampire only has minimum amount of Vitae immediately after the Embrace, right? So, if someone's Embrace happens shortly before dawn, then... such a character has smallchance of survival. Because such a character won't have many opportunities to feed before falling asleep... and then, he'd spend his remaining Vitae when waking up at sundown. So... immediate torpor?</div> </div> </div> </div>This probably wouldn't be a common situation. The Embrace takes major effort to put in for most vampires (a dot of Willpower in 1e, or Humanity in 2e, both of which cost experience to recover). Fledging a vampire involves vomiting a little piece of your undead self into them. A vampire has to be kind of stupid, kind of crazy, or in a panic to give the Embrace without preparation, and that includes leaving time aside to make sure your new undead investment learns the right protocol and doesn't immediately crumble away. Plus the later in the night it is, the less convenient it is to find living people walking around. Vampires are usually going to take care to Embrace early in the night, just as a practical matter. Even in extreme situations, nothing prevents the sire from spilling some of her own blood to feed the neonate. This may not be the ethical choice or even the wise choice, given the nature of the blood bond, but any port in a storm and all.<br /> <br /> Now, are there crazy, sadistic vampires out there invested enough in the idea to go Embracing on a whim without sticking around to attend to the fledgling's survival? There are; a few of the canonical NPC writeups, like Tzigane in Ancient Mysteries, were sired that way. (Tzigane's one of my favorites.) And there are other possible situations. The sire could be killed shortly after the Embrace, only for the killers to miss the childe. The draugr, the empty husks of vampire that remain when the Man has faded entirely and only the Beast rules, behave erratically and sometimes Embrace, and the childe doesn't necessarily rise as draugr. 2e introduces revenants, miserable consequences of careless overfeeding, weak half-vampires who rise undead sometimes after the Kindred exsanguinate a meal. Revenants are extra fucked, as not only do they not often have a sire sticking around to teach them the ropes, but until they can either convince a full Kindred to complete their Embrace, or hunt and drink one's soul, they have various extra limitations, like barely being able to retain stored vitae from night to night.<br /> <br /> So yeah, while uncommon, it can happen. In those cases, to keep things interesting, the risen neonate probably has the most basic instruction from the Beast within, so to speak. The new vampire has the simplest instincts: must feed, food doesn't do the job, hyperawareness of blood, an instinctive fear of fire and the sun, a temper that boils deep, maybe some instinctive expression of the power of the blood through healing or basic Disciplines. None of the specifics, no explanation why, no awareness of Kindred culture or society, nothing but hunches and guesswork. Just enough knowledge to be dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T11:55:58-07:00","id":672258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672254#post672254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Okay, so here's a million dollar question: why just not turn yourself in? Wouldn't a typical, moral person do just that, if she found out that she's been infected with a &quot;disease&quot; that makes her a danger to other? I would do that, personally...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's one of the reasons why there's a Tradition against siring vampires. If you just make vampires whenever and wherever you want, you risk the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> If a vampire was created and didn't have their sire, but also wasn't a more base revenant, and decided that with their lack of a pulse and desire for human blood they should go to the police or a hospital, they would likely either find themselves frenzying through hunger at some point, or eventually fall into daysleep where they would then be treated like a corpse and disposed of as corpses are. This is also why the Invictus and other organizations tend to have a hand in medical and law enforcement agencies, so that they can get a heads up whenever some fledgling decides to shake things up, so they can fix things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:15:27-07:00","id":672274,"title":"","content":"To quote Futurama: &quot;<i>being a robot's great, but we don't have emotions, and sometimes that makes me very sad.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The problem with roleplaying a character with muted emotions is that they also have a muted ability to give a shit about not having emotions. You can't remember what it's like to feel genuine happiness, but you don't really care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:33:21-07:00","id":672291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672274#post672274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To quote Futurama: &quot;<i>being a robot's great, but we don't have emotions, and sometimes that makes me very sad.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The problem with roleplaying a character with muted emotions is that they also have a muted ability to give a shit about not having emotions. You can't remember what it's like to feel genuine happiness, but you don't really care.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I kind of get the idea behind that &quot;dead inside&quot; thing. It's very subtle, but I like it...<br /> <br /> Coming back to the &quot;ignorant new vampire&quot; idea - please tell me, guys: what kind of punishment would a Prince typically use against a vampire that sired a childe and totally abandoned her in panic? Execution of the perpetrator and the progeny, like in <i>Interview With The Vampire</i>, or something else?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:42:49-07:00","id":672297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672291#post672291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know. I kind of get the idea behind that &quot;dead inside&quot; thing. It's very subtle, but I like it...<br /> <br /> Coming back to the &quot;ignorant new vampire&quot; idea - please tell me, guys: what kind of punishment would a Prince typically use against a vampire that sired a childe and totally abandoned her in panic? Execution of the perpetrator and the progeny, like in <i>Interview With The Vampire</i>, or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly execution of the sire. The progeny might be executed, or they might be offered for an upstanding member of the court to <s>use as a slave</s> adopt. That was actually almost the exact starting premise of the Masquerade video game. You played as a newly (and illegally) embraced neonate, whose sire gets executed for it in the opening cutscene. Then the Prince himself publicly announces his intention to take you in and raise you as his own. Of course, he promptly sends you on some crazy tasks with no instruction whatsoever as a test to prove you're worthy of his tutelage and you're left to figure stuff out mostly on your own, with a little assistance from some helpful NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:43:08-07:00","id":672300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672291#post672291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming back to the &quot;ignorant new vampire&quot; idea - please tell me, guys: what kind of punishment would a Prince typically use against a vampire that sired a childe and totally abandoned her in panic? Execution of the perpetrator and the progeny, like in <i>Interview With The Vampire</i>, or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're just some nobody and the Prince is secure in power, staking for a period of the sire or Final Death. If they need to make a show, Final Death. If it's someone they need, a public slap on the wrist with a behind the scenes, 'You owe me one,' and the myriad variations of that. The childe might be killed or placed under someone who could 'raise them right,' with bonus points gained for the Prince if it's to an enemy of the sire. If the childe seems willing to toe the line maybe just let it slide. Things could change if the childe vampire had done something like Embrace all their frat buddies or put a video of her recent changes on YouTube.<br /> <br /> In the novels, the Prince sired someone expressly against his own rules against Embrace, and in turn a vampire who didn't like him just sired someone and abandoned them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:09:49-07:00","id":672325,"title":"","content":"Abandoning a childer isn't really -quite- a direct sin, but I doubt anyone would look highly on it. Its like letting little kids play with matches - you know someone's going to get burned. And its going to be the parent's fault. An abandoned childer is just a Masquerade breach waiting to happen.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't know if the typical Carthians would execute either the sire or childer there. Or the Circle of the Crone (basically anarchists here). A typical Invictus or Lancea Prince almost certainly would, but I'm not convinced that the other Powers That Be would do that as a first resort. The Ordo Dracul in their domain could claim that abandoning a childer is part of an experiement and get off scott free. Too much depends on the local political structure. Invictus are the most typical rulers, but after that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:25:17-07:00","id":672332,"title":"","content":"My idea to handle a situation like this would be that the childe would, eventually, get dragged in front of the Prince. Then, the Prince would blood bond him for a year and kind of adopt him. Whether the blood bond would continue after the initial year would depend on the childe's further actions... As for the sire, I see him Embracing the childe after a feeding that went too far - so, I'd feel kind of sorry if this character got executed just for being merciful...<br /> <br /> Okay, I have one big request now: could you guys give me a short summary of the beliefs of Lancea Sanctum, Ordo Dracul and Circle of the Crone? The 1E rulebook is kind of frustrating in that matter, as it's very vague. It's mentioned that CotC are about acceptance and redemption, but it's not explained what does it mean exactly. It's said that LS are both penitent and scary predators, but again - what does it mean? And there's nothing said about OD's exact philosophy and modus operandi, aside from the general idea that they are vampire occultist / alchemists / researchers exploring the vampire condition. Overall, I have no idea how to portray these groups in-game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:47:56-07:00","id":672343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672332#post672332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea to handle a situation like this would be that the childe would, eventually, get dragged in front of the Prince. Then, the Prince would blood bond him for a year <b>and kind of adopt him.</b> Whether the blood bond would continue after the initial year would depend on the childe's further actions... As for the sire, I see him Embracing the childe after a feeding that went too far - so, I'd feel kind of sorry if this character got executed just for being merciful...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an exceptionally charitable and welcoming Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-20-2015, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:50:03-07:00","id":672344,"title":"","content":"The Lancea (et) Sanctum believe that vampires have a divine mission from God to be the wolves to his shepherd. They are supposed to prey upon humanity in order to keep them in line and drive them into the arms of the church. They believe their founder to be the biblical Longinus, the Roman soldier who pierced Christ's side with a spear. The LS believe that while doing this he accidentally ingested some holy blood straight from the source, and became a vampire as a result.<br /> <br /> Now, the Ordo Dracul have the basic mission statement of &quot;transcend the vampiric condition&quot;. Note that this is not the same as becoming human again. They want to keep all the perks but get rid of all the weaknesses that come with them. Their primary approach to this goal is to conduct experiments of questionable ethics.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone believe that the above two are doing it wrong, and that the best way to be a vampire is to just <i>be </i>a vampire. To revel in the power and the blood without trying to cleave to human values or tinker with the equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 09-20-2015, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T14:19:27-07:00","id":672362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672332#post672332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have one big request now: could you guys give me a short summary of the beliefs of Lancea Sanctum, Ordo Dracul and Circle of the Crone? The 1E rulebook is kind of frustrating in that matter, as it's very vague. It's mentioned that CotC are about acceptance and redemption, but it's not explained what does it mean exactly. It's said that LS are both penitent and scary predators, but again - what does it mean? And there's nothing said about OD's exact philosophy and modus operandi, aside from the general idea that they are vampire occultist / alchemists / researchers exploring the vampire condition. Overall, I have no idea how to portray these groups in-game...</div> </div> </div> </div>The typical Lancea Sanctum had a hierarchy and practices that emulate or mock the Roman Catholic Church. Their general premise is that you did something in life for God to damn you to existence as an undead blood drinking monster. You might be able to return to his grace or gain some kind of reward after Judgement Day if your predation on humanity turns them or keeps them on a path to God or convince and convert other vampires in the righteousness of their cause. Theban Sorcery is a gift granted to them from God to assist them in ensuring vampires think twice about mocking their calling and assist them in their divinely mandated role. How devout or impious the members are towards that agenda and the rituals varies from setting to setting.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone emulate human pagan blood cults that primarily (but not exclusively) serve a female deity, and typically elevate vampires to a religious status as the embodiment of their preferred deity or at least servants who share a higher level of communion with said goddess than humans could never reach. They don't have any uniform hierarchy or set of beliefs, as they tend to be more of a (perverted) interpretation of the primary interests of whoever they worship. Cruac is generally considered a blood magic gifted to servants of the local chapter's deity to provide insight and power to their practitioners.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul studies various facets of the vampiric condition and have developed a series of pseudo-scientific experiments, exercises, or meditation techniques to alter their own body sufficiently to make those vampiric powers function more efficiently permanently, called Coils of the Dragon. They have a byzantine hierarchy that revolves around the mentor student relationship in conjunction with the number of Coils they have proven to master with the penultimate objective of being able to completely transcend the vampiric condition into something else. How these changes are accomplished is not as important so long as they can be replicated by someone else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-20-2015, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T14:26:40-07:00","id":672365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672332#post672332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea to handle a situation like this would be that the childe would, eventually, get dragged in front of the Prince. Then, the Prince would blood bond him for a year and kind of adopt him. Whether the blood bond would continue after the initial year would depend on the childe's further actions... As for the sire, I see him Embracing the childe after a feeding that went too far - so, I'd feel kind of sorry if this character got executed just for being merciful...</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an excellent setup for a game. And in that context, I dont think the sire would necessarily need to be executed. It just depends on how sympathetic the powers that be are to the Sire's plight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672332#post672332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have one big request now: could you guys give me a short summary of the beliefs of Lancea Sanctum, Ordo Dracul and Circle of the Crone? The 1E rulebook is kind of frustrating in that matter, as it's very vague. It's mentioned that CotC are about acceptance and redemption, but it's not explained what does it mean exactly. It's said that LS are both penitent and scary predators, but again - what does it mean? And there's nothing said about OD's exact philosophy and modus operandi, aside from the general idea that they are vampire occultist / alchemists / researchers exploring the vampire condition. Overall, I have no idea how to portray these groups in-game...</div> </div> </div> </div>Gladly!<br /> <br /> The Invictus' philosophy centers around protecting the Masquerade. In 2e, one of their nicknames is &quot;the conspiracy of silence&quot;, because they infiltrate human power structures and use their influence to keep the herd under control. They also fancy themselves the spiritual successors to the Camarilla, and believe that gives them the right to rule over the dead as well, though in truth their reach is far less ubiquitous than they would have you believe.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum, or Lancea et Sanctum if you want to use proper Latin grammar, are the largest monotheistic Kindred religion. At its most fundamental, their dogma revolves around the belief that the Kindred condition is a curse from God. All vampires are inherently and irredeemably Damned, but that doesn't mean they don't have a place in God's plan. As God's chosen predators, they take it upon themselves to cull the flock.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone began as an association of various Poly-theistic vampires that banded together against religious persecution by the Lancea et Sanctum. They welcome vampires of any faith, so long as they uphold the organization's central ideal of religious freedom.<br /> <br /> The Carthians are to the Invictus as the Circle of the Crone are to the Lancea et Sanctum. A coalition of political dissidents united under the common ideal of political reform for Kindred. Anarchists, fascists, socialists, libertarians, communists, capitalists, you name it, all banded together because they can at least all agree that the current system doesn't work, even if they can't agree on a better alternative.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul follow the ideals of Dracula, who believed, as the Lancea et Sanctum believe, that he was Cursed by God. But rather than humbly accepting his role or seeking forgiveness, he sought to spit in the face of the God that Damned him. He sought not only to rid himelf of the Curse, but to add insult to injury, turning its weaknesses into advantage. Some modern Dragons share Dracula's belief that their condition is a Curse from God, others take a more scientific view, perhaps seeing it as a disease or mutation, and some are even agnostic about the nature of the condition. But all share the goal of rising above it and becoming something greater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-20-2015, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T15:21:31-07:00","id":672408,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info on covenants!<br /> <br /> To clarify something: which covenant is less cruel to humans? In the corebook, there's this suggestion that LS rejects humanity and sees the vampires as above humans. So, they seem to be more scary and cruel than CotC? Also, whom do the LS prey on - do they feed on sinners, or all humans with no distinction? What's the attitude of CotC in that matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T15:30:13-07:00","id":672411,"title":"","content":"If a newly Embraced vampire decides the best thing to do is walk into a police station and turn himself in (which I would consider pretty unlikely, but let's roll with it), if he's lucky he's going to be held in a holding cell and thought a complete whackjob until word gets up the chain to those in the know and he's released into the company of a blood-bound lawyer and shuffled in front of the Prince. Not the most prestigious beginning for a character, but nothing a little Dominate can't fix.<br /> <br /> If he's unlucky then something happens that forces the issue, like the sun coming up forcing him to sleep (or worse, burning him alive) or he attacks cops in a Frenzy, or a million other ways that can go wrong. Then even if he somehow escapes the police station, he's going to be pursued by the cops AND the local court for Masquerade breach, and his days are numbered.<br /> <br /> Also, one thing to keep in mind about executions in Vampire: there are probably plenty of places in the world where private executions are carried out via staking and giving the torpid Kindred to the elders who can only feed on Kindred blood. Who fears a blood bond to a truly dead man?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T15:43:25-07:00","id":672415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672408#post672408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the info on covenants!<br /> <br /> To clarify something: which covenant is less cruel to humans? In the corebook, there's this suggestion that LS rejects humanity and sees the vampires as above humans. So, they seem to be more scary and cruel than CotC? Also, whom do the LS prey on - do they feed on sinners, or all humans with no distinction? What's the attitude of CotC in that matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you want a covenant who's least cruel, you'd probably need to go with the Carthians. They, at the very least, recognize that they need to adapt to modern human society in order to survive in the world. The Lancea Sanctum view themselves as substitute Satans and that it is their divine mission to terrorize and punish sinners. The Invictus want to make themselves untouchable by ruling as much territory as they can. The Circle of the Crone uses magic that requires blood sacrifices and bodily mutilation, while the Ordo Dracul are focused primarily on becoming the perfect being.<br /> <br /> To clarify more on the LS, which I found out the core book is extremely vague about. In the Bible, the being known as Satan actually works for God and is specifically tasked with testing people's faith, punishing the sinful and strengthening the faithful. However as humanity became more and more abundant, Satan found his job to become increasingly difficult until he could no longer satisfy it on his own. The Lancea Sanctum picks up the slack, performing Satan's duties while on earth. They are Christian zealots who believe medieval justice is perfectly acceptable if it is carried out in the name of God.<br /> <br /> <br /> To answer one of your questions, yes, they do prey on sinners. They even like to embrace them sometimes as punishment. They are extremely protective of the pious and virtuous, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-20-2015, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:00:05-07:00","id":672433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672344#post672344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea (et) Sanctum believe that vampires have a divine mission from God to be the wolves to his shepherd. They are supposed to prey upon humanity in order to keep them in line and drive them into the arms of the church. They believe their founder to be the biblical Longinus, the Roman soldier who pierced Christ's side with a spear. The LS believe that while doing this he accidentally ingested some holy blood straight from the source, and became a vampire as a result.<br /> <br /> Now, the Ordo Dracul have the basic mission statement of &quot;transcend the vampiric condition&quot;. Note that this is not the same as becoming human again. They want to keep all the perks but get rid of all the weaknesses that come with them. Their primary approach to this goal is to conduct experiments of questionable ethics.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone believe that the above two are doing it wrong, and that the best way to be a vampire is to just <i>be </i>a vampire. To revel in the power and the blood without trying to cleave to human values or tinker with the equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>2nd edition is tweaking the covenants a bit.<br /> As for difference between the Crone and the Lance?<br /> My respected elder father of the Crone(yes that is a position in the Circle)explained it this way.<br /> &quot; The Circle is a spiritual path not a religion. The Lance is a religion.<br /> Religion is for those afraid going to hell! Spirituality is for those who have been there and back.<br /> Once you understand that, you understand the nature of our conflict.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:03:50-07:00","id":672434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672408#post672408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify something: which covenant is less cruel to humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're all mixed bags, and it can vary from domain to domain. All the covenants have more sympathetic contingents and more monstrous corners.<br /> <br /> <b>The Invictus</b> is probably the most moderate by this metric. Their nicer guys aren't as nice, but their nastier guys aren't as nasty. They're a very pragmatic lot, with an ideology arguably closest to the human perspective: they like stability and temporal power. Fuck you if you get in their way, but if you don't, they're usually content to leave you be. Made men, middle managers, power brokers and peacemakers. Ultimately they just want everything flowing smoothly and predictably so they can comfortably skim off the top.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lancea et Sanctum</b> are a modern religion. They have all the positives and all the drawbacks that implies. They believe in a just God and the sanctity of the righteous. Milder Sanctified might interpret this as a motive to protect innocent and upright mortals from the predations of the likes of the Invictus. More severe Sanctified view it as a ticket to visit horrors upon those they view inferior, and to put the devout through hell as a sort of &quot;test&quot; to weed out those whose faith isn't strong enough. The rank and file attendees of Midnight Mass lean upon the Spear as a comfort to themselves that their unlife drinking the blood of the living isn't so bad as they manage survival night by night.<br /> <br /> <b>The Carthian Movement</b> are extreme. From a mortal perspective, that can be good or it can be very bad. They believe in mortal ideologies applied to undead life, and that can encompass anything from democracy and rule by consent, to anti-coercive libertarianism, to socialist cooperation, to a fascist vanguard. When they're busy fighting the other covenants for influence over domain policy, they're a moderating force, at least as applies to mortals: Kindred society comes first, mortal affairs secondary. (Carthians are known for not being afraid of collateral damage when attacking other vampires' power bases, though.) When they take power and the other covenants consent to their ideas, they dive straight into the banality of evil, setting up systems and engines of industry to serve the people (vampires) with what they need to thrive and prosper (the blood of the living).<br /> <br /> <b>The Circle of the Crone</b> are a wild card. They're insular, and they value power, wisdom and willpower. They also value worshippers, who can probably expect to be treated the most kindly of any of the covenant's human servitors \u2013 keep in mind that's relatively speaking, now. They're iconoclasts, and other iconoclasts can usually expect to receive at least a mild nod of respect and be passed over. The rest of the herd, those who don't demonstrate power, wisdom or willpower in sufficient degrees to defend themselves? The acolytes don't hesitate to shed their blood in honor of their own glory.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ordo Dracul</b> is a small cult of psychonauts and experimenters, really only held together by one constant: they hate the Curse. Some of them hate it because they loved life, and want to climb back to something resembling it. Some of them simply chafe at any kind of restraint. The nicest saints of the Kindred are probably split between the Dragons and the Sanctified. The devils are here too. Members of the Order are secretive and practical, so they're unlikely to prey on humans in large numbers in most cases, but they're liars without restraint. A fiend of the Sanctified or the Acolytes will tear a human apart with a feeling of triumphant glory. A fiend of the Dragons will tear a human apart and feel nothing at all except mild curiosity. Which is worse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T18:39:18-07:00","id":672668,"title":"","content":"You really do have an entire spectrum across the covenants, it's easy to hold up the cruelest aspects of a covenant and consider them to be the 'most' cruel but they're all pretty equal if you just judge by the extremes. Every member of the every covenant is just as capable of committing almost any kind deed a mortal could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-20-2015, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T00:36:55-07:00","id":672967,"title":"","content":"So, if I understand correctly, the LS are about &quot;you became a vampire because you are a sinner, now you have to punish other sinners and feed on them&quot;, right? While CotC are &quot;vampires are a natural thing, it's okay to be a vampire&quot;?<br /> <br /> If so, are there any moral rules CotC subscribe to?<br /> <br /> Coming back to the subject of an illegal Embrace and punishment - what are some typical punishments in the Kindred society, aside from execution and Vinculum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T02:58:20-07:00","id":673035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672967#post672967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming back to the subject of an illegal Embrace and punishment - what are some typical punishments in the Kindred society, aside from execution and Vinculum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Staking for a determined period of time, mutilation with an added proibition to regrow the lost limb for a time, loss of pized possessions like territory...<br /> <br /> More personal, fucked-up punishments like &quot;I'm going to blood bond your sister and make your mother forget that you exists, for the good of the Masquerade and also because fuck you of course&quot; may occour.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T03:45:58-07:00","id":673046,"title":"","content":"There's also various Invictus Oaths and Carthian Law and rituals that can curse a transgressor in various ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T05:43:06-07:00","id":673087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672967#post672967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, are there any moral rules CotC subscribe to?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Circle of the Crone has a wide variety of beliefs but the most important one is being true to what you are, which is a vampire. Most of them appreciate moralities that go along with their natural inclinations rather than what humans consider moral.<br /> <br /> One of the Circle's many factions is the Second Descent, who believe that the dead and the living should not mix. Therefore they have three main 'rules.' No ghouls, no human allies, and only Embrace very rarely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T05:48:07-07:00","id":673089,"title":"","content":"I suspect they may be gone in second edition though, seeing as that's basically a recipe for flushing your Humanity down the toilet now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T05:57:51-07:00","id":673095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=673089#post673089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect they may be gone in second edition though, seeing as that's basically a recipe for flushing your Humanity down the toilet now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have human contact without them being allies. But the Circle was mostly about appreciating the differences between your human and vampire self, which are found through losing humanity. You don't want to go to 0 because then you can't appreciate the differences, but getting low is fine as long as you've learned from it. That said, I'd expect taking a bane for the 'time without human contact' sins would be an accepted and encouraged practice in some of the Circle of the Crone factions, as it's a very clear tradeoff between your humanity and vampire self.<br /> <br /> And of course second edition makes buying back vestiges of Humanity much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-21-2015, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T07:05:43-07:00","id":673146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672967#post672967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I understand correctly, the LS are about &quot;you became a vampire because you are a sinner, now you have to punish other sinners and feed on them&quot;, right? While CotC are &quot;vampires are a natural thing, it's okay to be a vampire&quot;?<br /> <br /> If so, are there any moral rules CotC subscribe to?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really, no. The Circle doesn't quite believe in evil the same way that other covenants do, so pretty much anything is open in theory. In reality, there are some standards that will shock the covenant, or draw more enemies, but nothing quite formalized. There are some actions that are considered to be too depraved to be vampire-as-natural-predator that many Crones won't abide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Coming back to the subject of an illegal Embrace and punishment - what are some typical punishments in the Kindred society, aside from execution and Vinculum? </div> </div> </div> Blood rent - having to provide herd for an elder. Loss of status and feeding grounds. Some kind of &quot;community service,&quot; often of the dangerous sort (plot point!). Enforced torpor for a period of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:07:34-07:00","id":673240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672967#post672967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I understand correctly, the LS are about &quot;you became a vampire because you are a sinner, now you have to punish other sinners and feed on them&quot;, right? While CotC are &quot;vampires are a natural thing, it's okay to be a vampire&quot;?<br /> <br /> If so, are there any moral rules CotC subscribe to?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hard to say. The CotC aren't just a unified religion or cult, they're a collection of many different pagan cults who have been categorized as a faction. Depending upon what cult you're dealing with, they could have radically different beliefs compared to another cult. Some may not even worship the Crone at all, but instead devote themselves to other ancient gods and goddesses. The example given in the core book tries to balance or offset the stagnant destruction vampires represent by taking up a hobby that promotes creation and growth, such as gardening or artistry.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone as provided in the core book believe that their goddess, The Crone, was the first vampire and the one who created beauty in the mortal world. Before she came to earth, mortals lived in a barren wasteland while the gods lived in paradise. She created paradise on earth as well, but drank the blood of others to increase her divine power and was eventually exiled from the heavens because of it. Vampires are her descendants and they share a portion of her divine power, or so the cult believes.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-21-2015, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:14:00-07:00","id":673245,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd like to say is that, much like the &quot;default&quot; Lancea et Sanctum is heavily drawn from Roman Catholicism, the &quot;default&quot; Circle of the Crone is heavily drawn from a vampire version of Wicca and neo-paganism. So, while it claims to be an ecclasitic collection of religions, its very much not the same as the old religions themselves. And some religions, such as voodoo, don't really fit in the Circle either, to the point we've seen new magic and organization associated with them in the books.<br /> <br /> Technically, the big uniting points of the Circle of the Crone are 1) a hatred of the Lance and 2) practice of Cruac. That said, pretty much everything else that the covenant shares, from history to outlook, is like a vampiric version of the modern neo-pagan movement. The goddess worship, the four archetypes, etc.<br /> <br /> And, like Wicca, the Circle doesn't make a claim that &quot;evil&quot; exists. However, there's a kind of code of conduct that floats around in their social circles (no pun intended).<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - that is not to say you can't have a different kind of Circle, but most of the material you'll see will reflect that stance. Just like you can adapt the Lance to reflect a different Christian denomination, or change the Ordo to reflect vampire-Buddhism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:51:45-07:00","id":673275,"title":"","content":"It's not as big or as formal a thing in Requiem as it is in Masquerade, but the Danse Macabre often works because of the series of favors and boons between participants. Common punishments probably can easily involve that, especially by making the transgressor owe a certain number of favors to the transgressed.<br /> <br /> The style and flavor of judgements can often depend on who rules it, though. A lax Invictus prince who plays it fast and loose to keep as many allies as possible is going to deliver quite a different degree of punishment than a prince the rules entirely through fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:55:28-07:00","id":673278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=672967#post672967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I understand correctly, the LS are about &quot;you became a vampire because you are a sinner, now you have to punish other sinners and feed on them&quot;, right? While CotC are &quot;vampires are a natural thing, it's okay to be a vampire&quot;?<br /> <br /> If so, are there any moral rules CotC subscribe to?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Do what thou wilt&quot; shall be the whole of the law. As a generalization, the Acolytes believe in growth and understanding more than they do straightforward morality. They're less interested in right and wrong than they are in strength and weakness, honesty and denial, freedom and constraint. Nicer Acolytes believe in these virtues for all beings, not just themselves, but so long as it doesn't set back another's spiritual growth, it is fit and right not to hold back from what you want and need. And hurting somebody doesn't always mean setting them back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:06:47-07:00","id":673302,"title":"","content":"One creative punishment that was used in a game I played in was for a newcomer to the city, a Deva with Striking Looks, who insulted a hideous Nosferatu, not realizing he was the Clan's priscus. Made him wear a featureless iron mask for a year and a day so he could experience going through his unlife without the advantage of a pretty face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:10:28-07:00","id":673305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=673302#post673302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Made him wear a featureless iron mask for a year and a day so he could experience going through his unlife without the advantage of a pretty face.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did he feed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:27:45-07:00","id":673312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=673305#post673305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How did he feed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, it was just before a 1 year time skip so we kind of glossed over the details. Maybe he had a small slit in the mouth and he had to be fed with a straw?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:44:05-07:00","id":673318,"title":"","content":"If he was a nosferatu or gangrel I could see him becoming like Vasagi the Suck, though that would probably take more than a year.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.brianlumley.com/graphics/artists/NecroArt18.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> But yeah, considering the 'immortal' nature of vampires there's a lot of punishments you can come up with. There's a nosferatu in Night Horrors who permanently disfigures vampires to be similar to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T16:45:03-07:00","id":673542,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the ideas on punishments!<br /> <br /> Re: Circle of the Crone. Hmmm... You know, based on what you guys say, these folks seem quite... unpleasant. Based on the corebook, I thought they seem to be the good guys (as opposed to LS' intolerance and the idea that vampires need to be inhuman monsters). But now it seems that the LS is less scary. CotC seems to promote vampirism as a good thing and not to have any moral rules...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T17:01:12-07:00","id":673588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=673542#post673542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the ideas on punishments!<br /> <br /> Re: Circle of the Crone. Hmmm... You know, based on what you guys say, these folks seem quite... unpleasant. Based on the corebook, I thought they seem to be the good guys (as opposed to LS' intolerance and the idea that vampires need to be inhuman monsters). But now it seems that the LS is less scary. CotC seems to promote vampirism as a good thing and not to have any moral rules...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, because a faction who requires blood sacrifices as a means to perform their magic really sounds like their moral compass points north. Rememeber, the Circle of the Crone are vampiric witches and warlocks, they wield blood magic and they worship ancient deities and spirits. It would not surprise me in the least to find a cult that devours people's hearts in order to absorb their strength. Knowing the CotC, they might actually be able to do so! If you want some more examples of what Cruac can do, turn to page 142 of the core book and enjoy. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> But the Lance can be just as terrifying, because Theban Sorcery allows them to perform twisted acts of biblical miracles. One of their abilities lets them afflict people with Stigmata, while another causes them to spew insects from their mouth whenever they tell a lie. You can find more information on that Discipline on page 145 - 149","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-22-2015, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T17:30:03-07:00","id":673650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=673542#post673542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Circle of the Crone. Hmmm... You know, based on what you guys say, these folks seem quite... unpleasant. Based on the corebook, I thought they seem to be the good guys (as opposed to LS' intolerance and the idea that vampires need to be inhuman monsters). But now it seems that the LS is less scary. CotC seems to promote vampirism as a good thing and not to have any moral rules...</div> </div> </div> </div>The covenants just give vampires a reason to go on. Whether they're all deluding themselves is up to you, but they're all trying to convince themselves of something. For the Lancea et Sanctum it's that God has a plan for them. For the Circle of the Crone it's that vampirism isn't a curse, it's a gift. The Invictus believe the baser instincts can be forestalled by rigid structure. The Carthians believe you can bring humanity into the equation. The Ordo Dracul believe they can overcome all the downsides of the condition and keep the upsides.<br /> <br /> Your character's moral compass is going to be decided by your character, not their covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T17:31:44-07:00","id":673653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=673542#post673542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Circle of the Crone. Hmmm... You know, based on what you guys say, these folks seem quite... unpleasant. Based on the corebook, I thought they seem to be the good guys (as opposed to LS' intolerance and the idea that vampires need to be inhuman monsters). But now it seems that the LS is less scary. CotC seems to promote vampirism as a good thing and not to have any moral rules...</div> </div> </div> </div>You sound like you're looking for a covenant to side with, as a player looking into the universe as opposed to a character inside it. You're not going to find one. <i>None of the covenants are the good guys.</i> To some extent, they can't possibly be, by their very nature. They're social clubs for vampires who drink the blood of the living. Everything about the covenants, their beliefs and practices, is structured to support vampires, make them feel better about drinking blood, and help them drink more blood.<br /> <br /> As a character, the covenants are there as a staff of solace to lean on, to ease you into life as a vampire and acclimate you to the Curse. They are all machines purpose-built to make men into monsters, because men can't survive as vampires, and monsters can. That's not to say they're malicious in intent. The majority of the members of the covenant really believe in what they're selling to you. Somebody sold it to them, too. And not all members of a covenant are monsters. Being a member of a covenant is ultimately counterproductive for a vampire who is trying to be an empathic, caring person, who if he can't be human can at least be humane. But people do counterproductive things all the time without recognizing the conflict, even when it's pointed out to them. That's very human.<br /> <br /> As a player, you shouldn't look at it as finding a covenant to root for or defend. Look for a covenant that inspires or grabs you. Look for one that's interesting, that draws out those conflicts in fun ways, and has a cool thesis underlying it that you can spin into a character you like. (And if it has a few twists or kinks that get in the way, feel free to push those aside. The covenants are broad and vary in interpretation from city to city and even from member to member. You don't have to be The Sanctified Guy to be A Sanctified Guy.)<br /> <br /> The covenants aren't there to be the good guys. If you're looking for the good guys, that's the PCs, friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T20:18:44-07:00","id":673820,"title":"","content":"From the VtR2e developer:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=501947#post501947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The assumption is that most heroic, tortured vampires will be PCs. So the All Night Society itself is pretty unpleasant, but struggling against it is absolutely a valid mode of play. And &quot;struggling&quot; can range from a <i>Blade</i>-style war to an attempt to reform one or more of the covenants.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the early part of <i>Forever Knight</i>, where Nick is a tortured hero, LaCroix is a villain, and Janette is a neutral party who caters to all elements of the vampire community, is a pretty viable setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T06:21:21-07:00","id":674114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=673588#post673588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, because a faction who requires blood sacrifices as a means to perform their magic really sounds like their moral compass points north. Rememeber, the Circle of the Crone are vampiric witches and warlocks, they wield blood magic and they worship ancient deities and spirits. It would not surprise me in the least to find a cult that devours people's hearts in order to absorb their strength. Knowing the CotC, they might actually be able to do so! If you want some more examples of what Cruac can do, turn to page 142 of the core book and enjoy. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> But the Lance can be just as terrifying, because Theban Sorcery allows them to perform twisted acts of biblical miracles. One of their abilities lets them afflict people with Stigmata, while another causes them to spew insects from their mouth whenever they tell a lie. You can find more information on that Discipline on page 145 - 149</div> </div> </div> </div>My favorite is kill your enemies servant then raise as an undead servant to mine him for information.<br /> Yet somehow in 2nd edition Theban has a Humanity requirement?<br /> I get Cruac rips your humanity more. But I cannot wrap my head around Theban requiring a Humanity equal to the level your casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T06:49:03-07:00","id":674128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674114#post674114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite is kill your enemies servant then raise as an undead servant to mine him for information.<br /> Yet somehow in 2nd edition Theban has a Humanity requirement?<br /> I get Cruac rips your humanity more. But I cannot wrap my head around Theban requiring a Humanity equal to the level your casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because the horror in Theban is supposed to be more intellectual than primal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T09:37:09-07:00","id":674347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674114#post674114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite is kill your enemies servant then raise as an undead servant to mine him for information.<br /> Yet somehow in 2nd edition Theban has a Humanity requirement?<br /> I get Cruac rips your humanity more. But I cannot wrap my head around Theban requiring a Humanity equal to the level your casting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And those are only a <b>couple examples</b> of each ritual or spell the Lance and Circle can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cruac (4) - Willful Vitae: Makes the ritualist temporarily immune to Blood Bonds and the effects of Vitae addiction upon consuming Vitae.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cruac (4) Tiamat Offspring: Creates a hormunculus using a variety of human parts<br /> <br /> <br /> Cruac (5) - A Child from the Stones: Creates a Gargoyle over a great and laborious crafting process.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cruac (5) - Roving Hut: Augments the ritualist's haven, allowing it to become supernaturally located, secure, or sized.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so the CotC is Requiem's new Tremere!<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------<br /> <br /> Theban (4) - Spear of Faith: Allows the caster to use the strength of their faith as a lethal weapon<br /> <br /> Theban (4) - Gift of Lazarus: Restores some life to a deceased target, turning them into a quickly decomposing zombie.<br /> <br /> Theban (5) - Damned's Day: Blots out the sun, reducing its effects from aggravated damage to lethal.<br /> <br /> Theban (5) - The Fruitful Womb: Causes a female to become pregnant with the caster's child, if they are mortal, or their own, if they are kindred.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-22-2015, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T10:12:26-07:00","id":674365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674114#post674114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get Cruac rips your humanity more. But I cannot wrap my head around Theban requiring a Humanity equal to the level your casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall the Doylist intent is to suggest that either that the Lancea's teachings have become warped, and they &quot;supposed&quot; (by whomever it is that supposes such things) to be more human/humane than they are - or that Theban sorcery has a different and more human/humane origin than the Lancea believes. Like if it was originally human magic, perhaps the Man needs to certain strength to use it, and too much influence by the Beast disrupts the mental state you need to be in.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T10:58:15-07:00","id":674396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674114#post674114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite is kill your enemies servant then raise as an undead servant to mine him for information.<br /> Yet somehow in 2nd edition Theban has a Humanity requirement?<br /> I get Cruac rips your humanity more. But I cannot wrap my head around Theban requiring a Humanity equal to the level your casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, it functionally Humanity Requirement are not that Different (you are your most powerful at Humanity 5 for either Ritual Magic system).<br /> For Cruac, and Rank 5 Ritual, your Humanity must be 5 or less (Max Humanity is 10-Ritual Level, or at least it used to be)...<br /> For Theban and Rank 5 Ritual, You must have Humanity of 5+. (Humanity Requirement of Humanity equal to Ritual)<br /> So in either form of Ritual, Humanity 5 is the sweet spot. <br /> <br /> You can be more of a Monster with Theban at the Lower Levels, while being more Humane with Cruac at the Lower Levels (very odd if you ask me)... Does this not strike people a little wrong?<br /> It Does Me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T11:04:03-07:00","id":674401,"title":"","content":"Not at all. God cursed the vampires to be predators with a noble purpose, not slavering beasts. Losing yourself to your baser nature makes you unfit to wield His power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T11:08:08-07:00","id":674404,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#00FF00\">It's almost as if finding a balance between your Humanity and your existence as a Vampire is a good thing.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">But that would only be possible if Humanity wasn't morality, right?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T11:57:20-07:00","id":674464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674396#post674396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet, it functionally Humanity Requirement are not that Different (you are your most powerful at Humanity 5 for either Ritual Magic system).<br /> For Cruac, and Rank 5 Ritual, your Humanity must be 5 or less (Max Humanity is 10-Ritual Level, or at least it used to be)...<br /> For Theban and Rank 5 Ritual, You must have Humanity of 5+. (Humanity Requirement of Humanity equal to Ritual)<br /> So in either form of Ritual, Humanity 5 is the sweet spot.<br /> <br /> You can be more of a Monster with Theban at the Lower Levels, while being more Humane with Cruac at the Lower Levels (very odd if you ask me)... Does this not strike people a little wrong?<br /> It Does Me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Uhh, in what world is raising people as a decaying zombie, blotting out the sun, or spontaneously impregnating women considered humane? Those are level 4 and 5 Theban Sorceries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T12:40:39-07:00","id":674481,"title":"","content":"I believe that you are missing my point... It would seem counterintuitive that Theban Sorcery should be viable at Humanity 1, but it is; Additionally, it is also a bit counterintuitive that you could practice Cruac at Humanity 9, but again, you can. See the issue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T12:48:09-07:00","id":674484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674481#post674481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would seem counterintuitive that Theban Sorcery should be viable at Humanity 1, but it is; Additionally, it is also a bit counterintuitive that you could practice Cruac at Humanity 9, but again, you can. See the issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. First off, that would just limit you to first rank rituals of either way. Second, the only way it would be an issue is if you somehow thought Theban sorcery represented only Humanity and Cruac the complete lack of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-22-2015, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T13:51:56-07:00","id":674564,"title":"","content":"It's pretty simple. Humanity isn't morality. It represents the relative strength of your Beast versus your Man. Theban draws its spiritual/magical strength from a vampire's Man. Cruac draws its spiritual/magical strength from a vampire's Beast. To do more potent Cruac rituals, you need a more potent Beast. To do more potent Theban rituals, you need a more potent Man. It's metaphysics, not morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:20:11-07:00","id":674586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674564#post674564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty simple. Humanity isn't morality. It represents the relative strength of your Beast versus your Man. Theban draws its spiritual/magical strength from a vampire's Man. Cruac draws its spiritual/magical strength from a vampire's Beast. To do more potent Cruac rituals, you need a more potent Beast. To do more potent Theban rituals, you need a more potent Man. It's metaphysics, not morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet at Humanity 5, you are capable of the pinnacle of either Blood Magic. *shakes head*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:32:22-07:00","id":674591,"title":"","content":"I don't think the potency of the Beast or Human matter much in this regard, actually. Cruac draws you more towards the Beast, evidenced by the lowering of the Humanity cap. You can have 5 dots of Cruac anywhere in that range. The Beast is in inherent to all vampires, unless you're using special rules. Theban just 'requires the careful, deliberate exercise of intellect and faith,' so need at least some Humanity going for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:07:28-07:00","id":674602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674586#post674586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet at Humanity 5, you are capable of the pinnacle of either Blood Magic. *shakes head*</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, if you have studied enough pagan blood magic to reach the pinnacle of Cruac, you're never coming back from this point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Balanced (Humanity 5-6): At this point, she\u2019s been around the block. ... She\u2019s seen pain and anguish as result of her condition, and is beginning to accept it as part of existence. She still has no issue relating to mortals; she just recognizes that she\u2019s never going to be one again. She\u2019s selfish, and lies like second nature. </div> </div> </div>and if you're this jaded and cynnical:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Weathered (Humanity 4): A weathered vampire has seen more death and devastation than most mortals will in a lifetime. ... While not spree killers, a vampire at this level has taken lives, and understands that he probably will again in order to guarantee continued survival. He sees humans as fragile and temporary. He\u2019s calculating and cunning, having a mind attuned to consequence. </div> </div> </div>you lack the faith required to perform miracles at the pinnacle of Theban Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:15:30-07:00","id":674605,"title":"","content":"Hell, I see Humans as Fragile and Temporary and &quot;stuff&quot;, and I would not call my &quot;Humanity&quot; or my &quot;Integrity&quot; a 4. Though they tend to work a bit better than 1st Edition's Morality Stats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:25:16-07:00","id":674619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674605#post674605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, I see Humans as Fragile and Temporary and &quot;stuff&quot;, and I would not call my &quot;Humanity&quot; or my &quot;Integrity&quot; a 4. Though they tend to work a bit better than 1st Edition's Morality Stats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're not a vampire and that's not what Integrity measures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T16:08:05-07:00","id":674667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674481#post674481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that you are missing my point... It would seem counterintuitive that Theban Sorcery should be viable at Humanity 1, but it is; Additionally, it is also a bit counterintuitive that you could practice Cruac at Humanity 9, but again, you can. See the issue?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well I can understand needing a low humanity to perform Cruac. Blood magic isn't exactly something a person would just choose to do. But Theban needing a high humanity contradicts what the Lancea are all about. They exist to punish the wicked and scare the righteous, they are substituting for Satan when he's over worked. Theban Sorcery inflicts biblical curses upon its victims, many of which are horrifyingly inhumane. Come to think of it, isn't there one that can turn a person into salt?<br /> <br /> The Lancea are Christians, yes, but they are <b>medieval Christians</b>, who can justify nearly anything as long as it's in the name of God or they feel that it's part of his will. They are fanatics and zealots, and the book actually states that in domains where they are the dominate faction, they have been known to launch crusades in order to wipe out heretics.<br /> <br /> The Lancea believe that pretending to be human is a sin and defies your role in God's plan. So I can't understand why their signature power would require you to have a high humanity.<br /> <br /> Actually, I may have to re-read the core book, because I don't remember there ever being a humanity requirement on either one of them. Cruac needed you to spend blood, while Theban Sorcery required you to sacrifice reagents of some sort. We are still talking about <i>1st edition</i> versions of these disciplines, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-22-2015, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T16:16:56-07:00","id":674673,"title":"","content":"No, 2nd edition. The post that kicked off this line of discussion was this one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674114#post674114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite is kill your enemies servant then raise as an undead servant to mine him for information.<br /> Yet somehow in 2nd edition Theban has a Humanity requirement?<br /> I get Cruac rips your humanity more. But I cannot wrap my head around Theban requiring a Humanity equal to the level your casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the reason Cruac has a minimum Humanity requirement is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it requires the careful, deliberate exercise of intellect and faith, Theban Sorcery requires the ritualist to have maintained his faculties. </div> </div> </div>As you lose Humanity, you become more bestial and more jaded, which would make it difficult to perform acts that require significant intellect and faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-22-2015, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T16:21:40-07:00","id":674676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674673#post674673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, 2nd edition. The post that kicked off this line of discussion was this one:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I see. Well the OP said earlier that he only has the 1st edition book (so do I), so I thought we were sticking to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T16:25:52-07:00","id":674677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674676#post674676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see. Well the OP said earlier that he only has the 1st edition book (so do I), so I thought we were sticking to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, strictly speaking this is a tangent. But it seems within the bounds of reasonable thread drift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T17:41:47-07:00","id":674700,"title":"","content":"Please don't drift! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T19:27:00-07:00","id":674799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674700#post674700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't drift! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wasn't trying to. I just missed the part where it switched to 2 ed rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T19:59:16-07:00","id":674861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674799#post674799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Wasn't trying to. I just missed the part where it switched to 2 ed rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not your fault, the talk of 2e rules is the part that was off-topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T07:15:13-07:00","id":675205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674619#post674619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you're not a vampire and that's not what Integrity measures.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as a 1st Edition Topic, we ARE talking about Humanity/Morality, and the fact that you can practice the brutal rituals of Cruac at Humanity 9 (and Theban at Humanity 1), even if at basic levels, is just crazy, if you ask me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 09-23-2015, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T08:13:53-07:00","id":675250,"title":"","content":"Well, it's likely you wouldn't <i>stay</i> at Humanity 9 for long if you were doing that regularly. <br /> <br /> But metaphysically, at Cruac 1 you've only got a bit of taint in you. It pulls you down, but not so much that you can't fight it and basically win. Not all level 1 rituals are harmful to anyone, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T09:55:08-07:00","id":675334,"title":"","content":"There's nothing moral or immoral about Cruac or Theban sorceries, calling Cruac brutal on its own is a misnomer. And while Humanity was much more closely entwined with Morality in first edition, it still was not just Morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-23-2015, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:06:17-07:00","id":675434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675334#post675334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing moral or immoral about Cruac or Theban sorceries, calling Cruac brutal on its own is a misnomer. And while Humanity was much more closely entwined with Morality in first edition, it still was not just Morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I fundamentally disagree here... Cruac is highly immoral in its practice and often its effects (there is a <i><b>reason </b></i>you cannot practice it at Higher Humanity). Assuming a Mortal practiced a variant that was accessible, their Morality would plummet. Especially when looking at 1st Edition...<br /> <br /> The new Edition has decoupled Morality from Practice, but still... I would call Cruac Immoral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:52:54-07:00","id":675565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675434#post675434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I fundamentally disagree here... Cruac is highly immoral in its practice and often its effects (there is a <i><b>reason </b></i>you cannot practice it at Higher Humanity). Assuming a Mortal practiced a variant that was accessible, their Morality would plummet. Especially when looking at 1st Edition...</div> </div> </div> </div>Cruac is no more or less immoral than disciplines or Theban sorcery. It requires Vitae to be used to get a desired effect, which is not always detrimental to people. It's a tool, like a scalpel or a car. The reason you cannot practice it at higher Humanity is because it is not associated with first edition's archaic beliefs of what high Humanity is, and instead moves with one's passion and will.<br /> <br /> Now if you think Cruac is immoral and should be changed, feel free to homebrew some exception to the rule. I'd probably suggest the Atrocity rules from Danse Macabre to look at first. But you've been told how it works in the books, and they can confirm it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-23-2015, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T12:56:21-07:00","id":675617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674114#post674114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite is kill your enemies servant then raise as an undead servant to mine him for information.<br /> Yet somehow in 2nd edition Theban has a Humanity requirement?<br /> I get Cruac rips your humanity more. But I cannot wrap my head around Theban requiring a Humanity equal to the level your casting.</div> </div> </div> </div> One last bit on this issue on the 2e rules. Chattnos, I think you're forgetting something rather crucial as part of the equation. Banes.<br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum and the Circle are equally &quot;monstrous.&quot; The Sanctified manifest that monstrocity through codes of acceptable monstrous behavior and developing aversions to holy days and the like, while the Acolites just drop Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:03:52-07:00","id":675649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675565#post675565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cruac is no more or less immoral than disciplines or Theban sorcery. It requires Vitae to be used to get a desired effect, which is not always detrimental to people. It's a tool, like a scalpel or a car. The reason you cannot practice it at higher Humanity is because it is not associated with first edition's archaic beliefs of what high Humanity is, and instead moves with one's passion and will.<br /> <br /> Now if you think Cruac is immoral and should be changed, feel free to homebrew some exception to the rule. I'd probably suggest the Atrocity rules from Danse Macabre to look at first. But you've been told how it works in the books, and they can confirm it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said it needed changing (nor did I say it was always detrimental), just that it was weird in the way it worked. It would make far more sense if they had slight tweaks to them... Such as No practicing Cruac at anything higher than Humanity 5, and you go down from there for each Rank available to you, or Theban only Working for those with 5+ Humanity, rather than 1+ Humanity.<br /> <br /> And since we ARE talking about 1st Edition, it IS ASSOCIATED with their archaic belief system. The Question revolved around 1st Edition (and 2nd Edition's Drift was a side conversation), since that was the only book the questioner had access to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes, Some of the Disciplines (and Theban) are just as immoral (Dominate and Majesty come immediately to mind, just to name two of them - though some have absolutely no moral component at all - the Physical Disciplines come to mind), in my opinion. Not sure how you can claim that taking total Control of someone's mind is not Immoral. Much like Ghouling is immoral and Addicting someone into slavery (Blood Bonding) is immoral, yet vampires do both routinely. Does not make those who practice such things Moral. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 09-23-2015, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:53:13-07:00","id":675687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675649#post675649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never said it needed changing (nor did I say it was always detrimental), just that it was weird in the way it worked. It would make far more sense if they had slight tweaks to them... Such as No practicing Cruac at anything higher than Humanity 5, and you go down from there for each Rank available to you, or Theban only Working for those with 5+ Humanity, rather than 1+ Humanity.<br /> <br /> And since we ARE talking about 1st Edition, it IS ASSOCIATED with their archaic belief system. The Question revolved around 1st Edition (and 2nd Edition's Drift was a side conversation), since that was the only book the questioner had access to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes, Some of the Disciplines (and Theban) are just as immoral (Dominate and Majesty come immediately to mind, just to name two of them), in my opinion. Not sure how you can claim that taking total Control of someone's mind is not Immoral. Much like Ghouling is immoral and Addicting someone into slavery (Blood Bonding) is immoral, yet vampires do both routinely. Does not make those who practice such things Moral. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In 1st edition Theban Sorcery didn't have a minimum Humanity requirement. As written, the <i>most</i> humane a master of Cruac can ever be in 1st edition is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s a tough world, and Kindred with this Humanity score accept that they need some toughness as well. Such characters can recognize and reject deliberate atrocities\u2026 but shit happens. If some happens to them, they throw it right back. Why should they act better than anyone else? At this Humanity, a Kindred starts to show the eerie unpleasantness that puts mortals on their guard. A skilled dissembler can still persuade mortals to ignore their instincts, though. </div> </div> </div>That seems perfectly reasonable to me. By your suggestion, simply learning a single level 5 Cruac ritual would leave you <i>permanently</i> like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forget sanity \u2014 at this Humanity, a Kindred can barely function as a sentient being. Little except a deranged obsession or direct threat to existence can focus the vampire\u2019s mind against the hungers of the Beast and the drive of an overwhelming Vice. The character even has trouble mustering the cunning needed to hide her crimes and debauches from mortal authorities or other Kindred. Rotting corpses strewn about a gore-spattered haven is a perfectly typical setting for such degenerate vampire. Mortals instantly recognize the Kindred as a monster whom they should flee, or at least a psychopath in the last stages of mental disintegration. </div> </div> </div>I don't know about you, but I think that sounds way too extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-23-2015, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:04:30-07:00","id":675690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675649#post675649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never said it needed changing (nor did I say it was always detrimental), just that it was weird in the way it worked. It would make far more sense if they had slight tweaks to them... Such as No practicing Cruac at anything higher than Humanity 5, and you go down from there for each Rank available to you, or Theban only Working for those with 5+ Humanity, rather than 1+ Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would only make sense that way if Cruac was immoral and Theban was moral or more human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And since we ARE talking about 1st Edition, it IS ASSOCIATED with their archaic belief system. The Question revolved around 1st Edition (and 2nd Edition's Drift was a side conversation), since that was the only book the questioner had access to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>It is associated with Morality, as I said. But it isn't Morality. Some of it is based on Morality, but it is not a matter of immoral or moral. It is a measure of ''the connection a Kindred feels to her leftover mortal feelings and to her capacity to empathize with other beings.' The flaw in first edition was that it went with a Victorian sense of ethics and degeneration that didn't match up with the modern world or what we know about human behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure how you can claim that taking total Control of someone's mind is not Immoral. </div> </div> </div>The same way I can claim that technology is not immoral. If you wish to talk more about morality, you can probably open a thread in the Off-Topic forum and maybe someone who wants to be judged by you will join in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T15:25:40-07:00","id":675744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=674114#post674114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get Cruac rips your humanity more. But I cannot wrap my head around Theban requiring a Humanity equal to the level your casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe if it were thought of as something to do with how much personal understanding of the Man or Beast the practitioner has, not just to what degree blood magic blocks or requires Humanity.<br /> <br /> IOW, it's possible to practice baseline Cruac at Humanity 9 because even the youngest Acolyte starts with a slobbering monster whose perversions can be turned outward, but which can also (usually) be tucked away when counterproductive. You let the Beast beat its chest for a minute, think bloody, brutal thoughts, and then when you're done you go right back to supressing it.<br /> <br /> The same young vampire would find baseline Theban Sorcery a comparative cakewalk, conceptually, because they've been listening to the Man before it was even the Man.<br /> ...an <i>old or degenerate </i>vampire, OTOH, one who's been dead several times longer than they've been alive, who has killed more times than they can remember, has been listening to the Beast so closely that the Man is becoming a reflex memory, would have it the other way around, would have to really scrape to find common ground with the LeS' mission plan of &quot;save and/or punish sinners for their own good/God.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, in OTHER other words, Theban Sorcery doesn't <i>require</i> you to be a good person, necessarily, any more than Cruac <i>requires </i>you to be a shameless monster - you just have to understand<i> what a</i> <i>good person would have done</i> <i>and why</i> before it'll work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 09-23-2015, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T17:09:52-07:00","id":675829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675687#post675687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1st edition Theban Sorcery didn't have a minimum Humanity requirement. As written, the <i>most</i> humane a master of Cruac can ever be in 1st edition is:<br /> <br /> <br /> That seems perfectly reasonable to me. By your suggestion, simply learning a single level 5 Cruac ritual would leave you <i>permanently</i> like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I think that sounds way too extreme.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I honestly don't see why Cruac is such a big deal on one's humanity. It's magic that uses blood as a fuel source.<br /> <br /> Big woop...<br /> <br /> <br /> You don't see Mages losing their shit when they conjure demons from the Stygian pits, or raise a zombie butler to clean their house.<br /> <br /> <br /> Magic is magic, it just depends on how it is used.<br /> <br /> <br /> Compare this to other powers the vampires have access to. Like, say, Protean. Which do you think is a bigger toll on one's humanity? Spilling a few drops of blood to protect a doorway, or sprouting claws and ripping a man to shreds with your bare hands?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dominate - turn people into mindless drones.<br /> <br /> Nightmare - invoke terror powerful enough to wound and kill.<br /> <br /> Majesty - convince people you're a god made flesh as they bow and kiss your feet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is one reason why I don't like 2nd edition much. A lot of the changes to setting and rules doesn't really make sense to me. I prefer 1st edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-23-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T17:25:00-07:00","id":675833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675829#post675829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic is magic, it just depends on how it is used.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on the setting and the system, and in WoD, particularly Requiem, it isn't true. Magic is belief and paradigm and sometimes spirits or gods or ghosts or Beasts or souls. Cruac draws power from the Beast, so you worldview must be that of the Beast, or at least close to it. Vitae is the medium through which the Beast affects the world. That's why Cruac uses Vitae. I'm unfamilair with 1e, honestly, but in WoD, magic is never just magic. It isn't in Mage, either. The cost is just something different.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T17:26:02-07:00","id":675834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675829#post675829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't see why Cruac is such a big deal on one's humanity. It's magic that uses blood as a fuel source.<br /> <br /> Big woop...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and its power comes from the Beast. That's why only vampires can do it. By learning more of it, you are distancing yourself from the human experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675829#post675829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't see Mages losing their shit when they conjure demons from the Stygian pits, or raise a zombie butler to clean their house.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom doesn't measure how far a mage is from human nature, and the Death arcana doesn't draw its power from Hubris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675829#post675829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic is magic, it just depends on how it is used.</div> </div> </div> </div>And low Humanity is just low Humanity. It doesn't mean you're a bad person, it just means you're not very much like a human. Granted, in 1e Humanity loss was often caused by violating a moral code, but even then it represented your connection to human nature, not moral standing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675829#post675829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare this to other powers the vampires have access to. Like, say, Protean. Which do you think is a bigger toll on one's humanity? Spilling a few drops of blood to protect a doorway, or sprouting claws and ripping a man to shreds with your bare hands?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dominate - turn people into mindless drones.<br /> <br /> Nightmare - invoke terror powerful enough to wound and kill.<br /> <br /> Majesty - convince people you're a god made flesh as they bow and kiss your feet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not <i>doing</i> Cruac that caps your Humanity, it's <i>knowing</i> Cruac. It has nothing to do with how moral or immoral the acts are, it's just the nature of the form of sorcery itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675829#post675829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one reason why I don't like 2nd edition much. A lot of the changes to setting and rules doesn't really make sense to me. I prefer 1st edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Cruac capped Humanity in 1e too. If anything, it makes more sense in 2e, where Humanity is less closely tied to Morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-23-2015, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T20:36:40-07:00","id":675986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675834#post675834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Cruac capped Humanity in 1e too. If anything, it makes more sense in 2e, where Humanity is less closely tied to Morality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh, so it does. Had to go back and re-read it to make sure because I didn't remember that being in there.<br /> <br /> So as I understand it, the knowledge and humanity cap are as such.<br /> <br /> Cruac 1 - Humanity 9<br /> <br /> Cruac 2 - Humanity 8<br /> <br /> Cruac 3 - Humanity 7<br /> <br /> Cruac 4 - Humanity 6<br /> <br /> Cruac 5 - Humanity 5<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, that's not really a big deal. Most vampires balance out around Humanity 4, while keeping something higher than 6 is considered rare for anything other than a fledgling. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T02:04:25-07:00","id":676207,"title":"","content":"Okay, okay! Let me ask another question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In 1E, there's Humanity, right? And some of it's basic sins are similar to mortal Morality. If so, then... how come that most vampires aren't extremely low on it? I mean: feeding might be considered a planned, serious crime akin to murder. Wouldn't that cause quick Humanity degeneration to all vampires..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T03:39:22-07:00","id":676273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675829#post675829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't see Mages losing their shit when they conjure demons from the Stygian pits, or raise a zombie butler to clean their house.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, binding ephemeral beings outside of their natural habitats is an act of hubris. So, if by &quot;losing their shit&quot; you mean suffering Wisdom loss, then yes, you do see just that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magic is magic, it just depends on how it is used. </div> </div> </div> I'm going to disagree. Awakened magic is different from vampiric blood magic, which is different from werewolf shamanism, which differs from sin-eater necromancy and fae glamour. And don't get me started on God Machine and Promethean alchemies. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Compare this to other powers the vampires have access to. Like, say, Protean. Which do you think is a bigger toll on one's humanity? Spilling a few drops of blood to protect a doorway, or sprouting claws and ripping a man to shreds with your bare hands? </div> </div> </div> Terrible example. Killing people is a Humanity breaking point in both editions of the game, and at a far lower level than 5, which is where Cruac caps at. The act of killing is the sin, not the act of using Protean. As well, acts of superhuman physical prowress is a breaking point as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dominate - turn people into mindless drones.<br /> <br /> Nightmare - invoke terror powerful enough to wound and kill.<br /> <br /> Majesty - convince people you're a god made flesh as they bow and kiss your feet. </div> </div> </div> The problem with your examples is that each one has nothing to do with the discipline itself. It has to do with the abuses vampires put them to. Wounding and injuring people are sins. As well, its not like the example Humanity breaking point list is exhaustive. &quot;Depriving another of consent with a Discipline&quot; is a breaking point at level 8; going further than that, such as your examples, would be a breaking point at lower levels as well. The example list is just that - examples. Gross abuses like the above would fall under Humanity breaking points if we follow the examples.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675744#post675744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, in OTHER other words, Theban Sorcery doesn't <i>require</i> you to be a good person, necessarily, any more than Cruac <i>requires </i>you to be a shameless monster - you just have to understand<i> what a</i> <i>good person would have done</i> <i>and why</i> before it'll work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theban doesn't require you to think like a good person in either edition. Its all about reaching out and channeling the power of God / angelic beings through rituals, which requires a rationale mind. Psychopaths are qualified in this case - they're very into base desires, but they're exceedingly rationale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675834#post675834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and its power comes from the Beast. That's why only vampires can do it. By learning more of it, you are distancing yourself from the human experience.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nitpick - we have examples of ghouls and, in some cases, specific bloodlines using blood magic. The former in the ghoul book, the latter in the Blasphemies and Sacraments book. Not sure what it means, its been a while since looking over them. But they're special cases, I imagine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not <i>doing</i> Cruac that caps your Humanity, it's <i>knowing</i> Cruac. It has nothing to do with how moral or immoral the acts are, it's just the nature of the form of sorcery itself. </div> </div> </div>Actually, fairly sure I'm going to disagree with this. There's been discussion and examples of people that walk away from Cruac and its degenerative effects. So, its use is definitely tied into the matter somehow, since its rejection helps lift the cap. I'm fairly sure, though I could be mistaken. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676207#post676207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, okay! Let me ask another question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In 1E, there's Humanity, right? And some of it's basic sins are similar to mortal Morality. If so, then... how come that most vampires aren't extremely low on it? I mean: feeding might be considered a planned, serious crime akin to murder. Wouldn't that cause quick Humanity degeneration to all vampires..?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a pretty extreme association. The vast majority of people don't consider all feeding to be on the same par as murder. Especially when your victim walks away alive. <br /> <br /> There's been plenty of debate on where feeding fits on the scale. Everyone runs things differently, so you'll have osme that refuse to make it a sin, some that treat how you feed as a potential sin (ie seduction and consent wouldn't be while a mugging would), and some that rule all feedings are a sin at some level. I've never seen anyone put it at the same level as murder, however. Not without actually draining a person dry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T04:57:43-07:00","id":676309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676207#post676207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, okay! Let me ask another question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In 1E, there's Humanity, right? And some of it's basic sins are similar to mortal Morality. If so, then... how come that most vampires aren't extremely low on it? I mean: feeding might be considered a planned, serious crime akin to murder. Wouldn't that cause quick Humanity degeneration to all vampires..?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because feeding isn't considered a planned and serious crime akin to murder unless you're planning on feeding on someone until they die. Which most vampires don't do, because they appreciate that if they don't drink people to death all the time, they'll be able to make it last for potentially centuries.<br /> <br /> It was also implied that characters would buy back their Humanity at certain points though I'm not sure how often that panned out during actual games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T05:48:03-07:00","id":676325,"title":"","content":"The book actually gives <i>accidentally </i>draining someone dry as an example of a sin one step higher, so merely feeding (which the character had already done and would therefore trump the manslaughter if it counted) is most certainly <b>not</b> Humanity 3 by any stretch of the imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T06:53:46-07:00","id":676353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675690#post675690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same way I can claim that technology is not immoral. If you wish to talk more about morality, you can probably open a thread in the Off-Topic forum and maybe someone who wants to be judged by you will join in.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you trying to convince me that Slavery (you know, Blood Bonding, Ghouling and Domination) is Moral? Or even Amoral? Because that is what it sounds like. My point is that whether YOU believe it to be a non-moral issue (in the game) is irrelevent, many people (in the game) would claim otherwise. There is no way you can convince me that much of what makes Vampire enjoyable is not immoral on some level. Just because the game does not care to make judgments upon such things (because it is a game after all) does not mean those actions are pure as driven snow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T06:56:10-07:00","id":676354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676273#post676273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick - we have examples of ghouls and, in some cases, specific bloodlines using blood magic. The former in the ghoul book, the latter in the Blasphemies and Sacraments book. Not sure what it means, its been a while since looking over them. But they're special cases, I imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in 2e, Ghouls specifically can't use any Discipline powers that require them to spill their Vitae, so they would definitely have to be a special case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676273#post676273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, fairly sure I'm going to disagree with this. There's been discussion and examples of people that walk away from Cruac and its degenerative effects. So, its use is definitely tied into the matter somehow, since its rejection helps lift the cap. I'm fairly sure, though I could be mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, by the rules, learning Cruac is what gives you the Humanity cap. Some practitioners might encounter Breaking Points as a result of things they do as part of the rituals, and they might be able to regain that lost Humanity when they walk away. But you don't have do perform a single ritual to get the cap, you just have to buy the dots, and there's no way to get rid of that cap by the rules. Of course, you can always make some kind of quest for redeption into the focus of a Story and raise or remove the cap through ST fiat, but I was talking about the standard Kindred experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676207#post676207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, okay! Let me ask another question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In 1E, there's Humanity, right? And some of it's basic sins are similar to mortal Morality. If so, then... how come that most vampires aren't extremely low on it? I mean: feeding might be considered a planned, serious crime akin to murder. Wouldn't that cause quick Humanity degeneration to all vampires..?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most vampires who live a long time <i>do</i> end up with pretty low Humanity. A lot of things that vampires naturally do causes Degeneration/Breaking Points, even more so in 2e where the scale is based less on Morality and more on doing inhuman things. This is by design; vampires are not a human, so maintaining their Humanity is naturally an uphill battle.<br /> <br /> As others have pointed out, most vampires don't feed their victims dry, so it's usually not on the same level as murder. That said, feeding can be (and often is) a Degeneration check or a Breaking Point, the level just depends on how you go about it. But ultimately, you <i>will</i> lose Humanity eventually, it's in your nature as a monster. That's a big part of the personal horror of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:00:36-07:00","id":676358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675687#post675687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about you, but I think that sounds way too extreme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, it was just a thought. Like I said, it just strikes me as a bit weird is all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:00:59-07:00","id":676359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676353#post676353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are you trying to convince me that Slavery (you know, Blood Bonding, Ghouling and Domination) is Moral? Or even Amoral? Because that is what it sounds like. My point is that whether YOU believe it to be a non-moral issue (in the game) is irrelevent, many people (in the game) would claim otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you can infer from my post I was talking about Dominate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no way you can convince me that much of what makes Vampire enjoyable is not immoral on some level. Just because the game does not care to make judgments upon such things (because it is a game after all) does not mean those actions are pure as driven snow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for warning me about how open minded you are. If you must know, I don't believe you can attribute your own morality to vampires, because they're not human. They are fundamentally different, and require fundamentally different things to exist. They have tools to help their existence, and however they use those tools can determine if the individual is a 'moral' or 'immoral' vampire, but the Disciplines and sorceries and even Vinculum are tools and have no morality on their own.<br /> <br /> This is, incidentally, the fundamental argument between the Lancea et Sanctum and the Circle of the Crone. One believes god is punishing them and making them act as demons on Earth and that their state is inherently bad. The other believes vampirism is a natural part of existence and one must embrace their new life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-24-2015, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:03:50-07:00","id":676363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676207#post676207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, okay! Let me ask another question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In 1E, there's Humanity, right? And some of it's basic sins are similar to mortal Morality. If so, then... how come that most vampires aren't extremely low on it? I mean: feeding might be considered a planned, serious crime akin to murder. Wouldn't that cause quick Humanity degeneration to all vampires..?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, most vampires stabilize around Humanity 4-5, in 1st Edition. It takes real effort to stay above that (I prefer the 6-7 range, personally). I have seen an occasional vampire climb as high as Humanity 8, but staying there is really difficult. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:20:08-07:00","id":676366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676359#post676359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you can infer from my post I was talking about Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really couldn't , which is why I said what I did. No worries, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks for warning me about how open minded you are. </div> </div> </div>Not sure where you are going with this. Are you implying that I am not? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you must know, I don't believe you can attribute your own morality to vampires, because they're not human. They are fundamentally different, and require fundamentally different things to exist. They have tools to help their existence, and however they use those tools can determine if the individual is a 'moral' or 'immoral' vampire, but the Disciplines and sorceries and even Vinculum are tools and have no morality on their own.<br /> <br /> This is, incidentally, the fundamental argument between the Lancea et Sanctum and the Circle of the Crone. One believes god is punishing them and making them act as demons on Earth. The other believes vampirism is a natural part of existence and one must embrace their new life. </div> </div> </div>That may be so... Vampires commit horrible acts on a daily basis. My point is that many of those very acts are immoral by their very nature (and yes, by Human Standards). Of course a Vampire does not care about such things most of the time, as he does them to survive, but that does not remove the immorality of those actions. Some actions are inherently immoral. I return to the big three... Blood Bonding, Ghouling and Dominate (and lets throw in the Embrace and Daily Feeding as well, just because I am interested in seeing how you define them as morally agnostic). In my opinion, all are inherently Immoral, on some level (and yes, Vampires do them anyways). Yes, there are some vampiric abilities that are not inherently immoral, and many of THOSE can BE immoral depending upon their use.<br /> <br /> Just because a Vampire believes he is a natural predator and is above such petty things as morality does not make him right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:27:51-07:00","id":676369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676366#post676366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because a Vampire believes he is a natural predator and is above such petty things as morality does not make him right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, the fact that a vampire is a natural predator and can form their own sense of morality is what makes them right. Just like you can enjoy your life without needing to drink people's blood to survive and being able to consider animals and plants 'totally different,' and thus okay to butcher and eat because your view of morality is one you've molded to make your own existence more palatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:50:21-07:00","id":676383,"title":"","content":"Feeding a little daily is the morally better option because the alternative is to starve yourself, randomly snap, and drain some poor git dry. <br /> <br /> The morally better option is the one where nobody dies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:54:46-07:00","id":676386,"title":"","content":"I mean, this is a debate between moral relativism and moral objectivism. If centuries of philosophy haven't been able to reconcile them, I don't think we will be able to do so here. What we can say about vampires is that they are not human, and that much of what they do naturally causes harm to humans. Should they be judged by the same moral standard we humans set for ourselves? That question probably doesn't have one right answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T20:11:43-07:00","id":677192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676207#post676207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, okay! Let me ask another question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In 1E, there's Humanity, right? And some of it's basic sins are similar to mortal Morality. If so, then... how come that most vampires aren't extremely low on it? I mean: feeding might be considered a planned, serious crime akin to murder. Wouldn't that cause quick Humanity degeneration to all vampires..?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The lower your humanity is, the worse deed you need to do in order to reduce it further. At humanity 10, you only need to have a stray, selfish thought or desire to degenerate to 9. At humanity 3 you need to commit mass murder, or brutally torture somebody for your entertainment. It's hard for a vampire to maintain a high humanity, but it's not impossible for them to find some level of balance.<br /> <br /> Like good ol Jack once said, &quot;don't be a homicidal maniac.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T20:22:17-07:00","id":677198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676273#post676273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, binding ephemeral beings outside of their natural habitats is an act of hubris. So, if by &quot;losing their shit&quot; you mean suffering Wisdom loss, then yes, you do see just that.<br /> <br /> I'm going to disagree. Awakened magic is different from vampiric blood magic, which is different from werewolf shamanism, which differs from sin-eater necromancy and fae glamour. And don't get me started on God Machine and Promethean alchemies.<br /> <br /> Terrible example. Killing people is a Humanity breaking point in both editions of the game, and at a far lower level than 5, which is where Cruac caps at. The act of killing is the sin, not the act of using Protean. As well, acts of superhuman physical prowress is a breaking point as well.<br /> <br /> The problem with your examples is that each one has nothing to do with the discipline itself. It has to do with the abuses vampires put them to. Wounding and injuring people are sins. As well, its not like the example Humanity breaking point list is exhaustive. &quot;Depriving another of consent with a Discipline&quot; is a breaking point at level 8; going further than that, such as your examples, would be a breaking point at lower levels as well. The example list is just that - examples. Gross abuses like the above would fall under Humanity breaking points if we follow the examples.<br /> Theban doesn't require you to think like a good person in either edition. Its all about reaching out and channeling the power of God / angelic beings through rituals, which requires a rationale mind. Psychopaths are qualified in this case - they're very into base desires, but they're exceedingly rationale.<br /> <br /> Nitpick - we have examples of ghouls and, in some cases, specific bloodlines using blood magic. The former in the ghoul book, the latter in the Blasphemies and Sacraments book. Not sure what it means, its been a while since looking over them. But they're special cases, I imagine.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, fairly sure I'm going to disagree with this. There's been discussion and examples of people that walk away from Cruac and its degenerative effects. So, its use is definitely tied into the matter somehow, since its rejection helps lift the cap. I'm fairly sure, though I could be mistaken.<br /> <br /> That's a pretty extreme association. The vast majority of people don't consider all feeding to be on the same par as murder. Especially when your victim walks away alive.<br /> <br /> There's been plenty of debate on where feeding fits on the scale. Everyone runs things differently, so you'll have osme that refuse to make it a sin, some that treat how you feed as a potential sin (ie seduction and consent wouldn't be while a mugging would), and some that rule all feedings are a sin at some level. I've never seen anyone put it at the same level as murder, however. Not without actually draining a person dry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 - Well I was kind of thinking of the Warlocks at the time, but I guess I misunderstood how they work.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - So far as I know, God Machine doesn't exist in first edition and I wouldn't include it even if it did.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3 - I don't think you need to kill a bunch of people to use Cruac though. It only takes a few points of Vitae and apparently you can use your own blood to fuel it. I didn't see anything that suggests you're sacrificing people on a routine basis to cast your spells.<br /> <br /> <br /> 4 - I fail to see how you can look at Dominate and not automatically call its power abusive. You have the power to tamper with people's memories, weaken or even completely destroy their autonomy, or you can even possess their body and take over their life! All three of those are crossing some pretty massive ethical lines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T20:36:51-07:00","id":677202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=677198#post677198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - So far as I know, God Machine doesn't exist in first edition and I wouldn't include it even if it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>The World of Darkness, p27. 'The god-machine built our world as a resting place for its First Children, whom men called angels or Ancient Ones.' There's a lot more. Like idigam, it didn't get expanded upon until much later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T21:13:56-07:00","id":677212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=677198#post677198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far as I know, God Machine doesn't exist in first edition and I wouldn't include it even if it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally the first thing written in the 1e core book is a story about it. There have been various allusions to it though out the run of 1e, the God Machine Chronicle merely expanded on the existing idea, just like the Strix Chronicle expanded on the already existing idea of the Strix, the Idigam expanded on the already existing idea of the Idigam, etc. It has always been and still is entirely optional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675829#post675829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 - I don't think you need to kill a bunch of people to use Cruac though. It only takes a few points of Vitae and apparently you can use your own blood to fuel it. I didn't see anything that suggests you're sacrificing people on a routine basis to cast your spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you did, that wouldn't be a reason for it to cap your Humanity. That would just cause Degeneration rolls/Breaking Points. It caps your Humanity because in order to perform Cruac, you need to have a certain connection with your Beast, and a person so in tune with their monstrous nature, by definition, cannot have high Humanity. Or at least, not <i>as</i> high as someone who aligns themselves with the Man more than the Beast can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675829#post675829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 - I fail to see how you can look at Dominate and not automatically call its power abusive. You have the power to tamper with people's memories, weaken or even completely destroy their autonomy, or you can even possess their body and take over their life! All three of those are crossing some pretty massive ethical lines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity isn't about ethics. Many things that cause Humanity loss are unethical (especially in 1e), but that's not what Humanity itself represents. If you destroy someone's autonomy and lose Humanity, you lost it because destroying autonomy is not a thing humans typically do, not because it's morally wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T21:36:14-07:00","id":677220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=677202#post677202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The World of Darkness, p27. 'The god-machine built our world as a resting place for its First Children, whom men called angels or Ancient Ones.' There's a lot more. Like idigam, it didn't get expanded upon until much later.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, it's in first edition core book? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T21:40:52-07:00","id":677225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=677220#post677220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, it's in first edition core book? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I believe it comes up clearly in Mage and Promethean, too. Someone gathered all the references when second edition came out but I'm not sure where.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T23:27:41-07:00","id":677362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=677225#post677225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. I believe it comes up clearly in Mage and Promethean, too. Someone gathered all the references when second edition came out but I'm not sure where.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots and lots of very brief and vague references. Tome of the Watchtowers, Saturnine Night, Mysterious Places, Urban Legends, The Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> To be fair, though, the God-Machine Chronicle and Demon: the Descent did a huge job reimagining it. What came out the other end is much more gameable than the extremely vaguely defined references that came before, but pretty different in nature and tone.<br /> <br /> Kind of lost track of what the topic is that's being discussed anymore, though, esp. since as stated, Cruac's relationship to Humanity hasn't changed much between first and second edition. The Humanity cap was always there. The breaking point for learning Cruac is new, but more reflects differences in 2e's view of Humanity than 2e's view of Cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T04:36:16-07:00","id":677488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=676354#post676354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in 2e, Ghouls specifically can't use any Discipline powers that require them to spill their Vitae, so they would definitely have to be a special case.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I was thinking 1e, since the two books I referenced were 1e books. Either way, the point I was kinda making was that I dont think we should make such hard-and-fast rules when there are exceptions to it. Same with the Cruac cap. I just don't like making generalities when we have outliers that defy said generalities.<br /> <br /> I personally believe the humanity cap exists because each casting of a ritual IS a breaking point. However, the assumption is that you'll be casting multiple rituals at that level, especially in teh course of learning that level, so instead of bogging down the game with multiple rolls for degeneration, simply assume you'll eventually fail and won't act in a way to raise your Humanity back up (ie, you'll still be using the magic at that level). So, I have to disagree with your idea on how Cruac and the cap work, Charlaquin.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=677198#post677198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Well I was kind of thinking of the Warlocks at the time, but I guess I misunderstood how they work.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was talking about anyone casting any spell, be it ghost, astral entity, fae, demon, you name it. All mages, irregardless of Path, would have that same &quot;going insane with power&quot; problem from your examples. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 - So far as I know, God Machine doesn't exist in first edition and I wouldn't include it even if it did. </div> </div> </div> I simply brought it up as a general &quot;these magics are not all the same.&quot; It doesn't matter if you include the God Machine or not. Awakened magic is not the same as any other game's magic, with the arguable potential exception of Mummy magic (a discussion for another thread).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3 - I don't think you need to kill a bunch of people to use Cruac though. It only takes a few points of Vitae and apparently you can use your own blood to fuel it. I didn't see anything that suggests you're sacrificing people on a routine basis to cast your spells. </div> </div> </div> Then, why did you bring up a comparison to murder in the first place? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4 - I fail to see how you can look at Dominate and not automatically call its power abusive. You have the power to tamper with people's memories, weaken or even completely destroy their autonomy, or you can even possess their body and take over their life! All three of those are crossing some pretty massive ethical lines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div> First, Dominate can be used in positive ways. Helping people forget trauma is arguably beneficial. Using it to protect the Masquerade when the alternative is worse? Possession can be used on willing targets. The old level 4 power was pretty bad, but MET altered it so that it didn't remove personality, so that's another consideration. None of that is crossing any lines I'm not comfortable with. Power is just that - power. A tool. The fact its very easy to use in a corrupt way is a different matter entirely. Vampires want to be tempted to use it, then start slipping down a slide into depravity. Part of the game.<br /> <br /> Two, Humanity is not the same as morals or ethics. Also, who's ethics are we talking about? Ethics are tied to specific societies, and vampires don't have ethics against using Dominate against others. Human society doesn't have mind control on this level, so clearly we don't have the ethics to reflect it. Mage society doesn't apply. So, who's drawing these theoretical ethical lines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T08:11:18-07:00","id":677629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=677488#post677488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, I was thinking 1e, since the two books I referenced were 1e books. Either way, the point I was kinda making was that I dont think we should make such hard-and-fast rules when there are exceptions to it. Same with the Cruac cap. I just don't like making generalities when we have outliers that defy said generalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=677488#post677488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally believe the humanity cap exists because each casting of a ritual IS a breaking point. However, the assumption is that you'll be casting multiple rituals at that level, especially in teh course of learning that level, so instead of bogging down the game with multiple rolls for degeneration, simply assume you'll eventually fail and won't act in a way to raise your Humanity back up (ie, you'll still be using the magic at that level). So, I have to disagree with your idea on how Cruac and the cap work, Charlaquin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'll just have to agree to disagree on that one. A cap on maximum humanity is just so functionally unlike Breaking Points that I can't see this being the intent. Especially because if this was the case you could just take a Bane for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T08:22:42-07:00","id":677647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=677629#post677629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'll just have to agree to disagree on that one. A cap on maximum humanity is just so functionally unlike Breaking Points that I can't see this being the intent. Especially because if this was the case you could just take a Bane for it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I figured you would. I mostly posted it to show why I disagree with you - we have fundamentally different takes on the issue in question. I simply can't agree with any of your conclusions when we have incompatable basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T07:05:34-07:00","id":678970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=675744#post675744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same young vampire would find baseline Theban Sorcery a comparative cakewalk, conceptually, because they've been listening to the Man before it was even the Man.<br /> ...an <i>old or degenerate </i>vampire, OTOH, one who's been dead several times longer than they've been alive, who has killed more times than they can remember, has been listening to the Beast so closely that the Man is becoming a reflex memory, would have it the other way around, would have to really scrape to find common ground with the LeS' mission plan of &quot;save and/or punish sinners for their own good/God.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, in OTHER other words, Theban Sorcery doesn't <i>require</i> you to be a good person, necessarily, any more than Cruac <i>requires </i>you to be a shameless monster - you just have to understand<i> what a</i> <i>good person would have done</i> <i>and why</i> before it'll work.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense but that makes no sense. Theban will raise your enemy's servant and turn him into a shambling dead thing so you can pump him for information.<br /> Where Man in that.<br /> I know the fluff says cruac is dark. But is it really darker than theban so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T07:24:12-07:00","id":678997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/649866-two-questions-from-a-vampire-newbie?p=678970#post678970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No offense but that makes no sense. Theban will raise your enemy's servant and turn him into a shambling dead thing so you can pump him for information.<br /> Where Man in that.<br /> I know the fluff says cruac is dark. But is it really darker than theban so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity isn't about light versus dark, it's about civilized versus primal. Theban may be dark, but it's dark in a sophisticated, calculating way. Cruac is dark in a raw, animalistic way. One requires you to embrace the Beast and act on instinct, the other requires you to maintain your faculties and employ your higher brain functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-26-2015, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T10:33:12-07:00","id":679164,"title":"","content":"I think Chattnos was pointing out that higher Humanity doesn't give bonuses to Theban. So if you're a Cleaver and only ingest blood of animals mixed in with normal food and you have a night job and eschew politics and don't even learn any disciplines, you have the same ability to use Theban rituals as a vampire who was kicked out of Belial's Brood for being too extreme and who strix envy. As long as they have one Humanity, they're set. In first edition, at least.<br /> <br /> That's because it's all it takes. Some mental faculties the Beast can't interrupt.<br /> <br /> In second edition the Humanity bar for learning rituals is higher. I imagine that's to offer a mechanical representation for how your mind is less harried by the Beast at higher Humanities.<br /> <br /> But also some people often associate Theban with good and Cruac with evil. Just as they associated the Lancea et Sanctum with good and the Circle of the Crone with evil. When both are organizations and lack an alignment at all beyond their amoral belief system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-26-2015, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}